hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"10201","10173/2 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated, Israil reported, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad and Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) giving the salutation to his right until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; and to his left the like of that."
"10202","10174 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sahl al-Ahwazi narrated, Imran ibn Musa narrated, from Sufyan, from Mughirah, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to give the salutation to his right and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah."
"10203","10175 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated, Shuayb ibn Ishaq narrated, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated, from Khalid ibn Maymun, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give the salutation to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen."
"10204","10176 - al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan al-Wasiti narrated, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad and Alqamah and Masruq and Abidah al-Salmani, from Abdullah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) giving the salutation: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen; and on the other side the like of that."
"10205","10177 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar and al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: Of what I have forgotten, I have not forgotten of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to give the salutation to his right: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen; and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen."
"10206","10178 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Jabir, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: Of what I have forgotten, I have not forgotten of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to give the salutation to his right and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah."
"10207","10179 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Humayd al-Tawil narrated, Shubah narrated, from Jabir, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give the salutation to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his face could be seen, or appear. Of what I have forgotten, I have not forgotten: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah."
"10208","10180 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: Of what I have forgotten, I have not forgotten of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to give the salutation to his left."
"10209","10181 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from Ibrahim, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give the salutation to his right: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; and to his left the like of that, until his cheek could be seen by them."
"10210","10182 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated, Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated, from Hajjaj, from al-Shabi and Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give the salutation to his right and to his left, turning the side of his face toward them."
"10211","10183 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated, Hafs ibn Jumay narrated, from Mughirah, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give the salutation to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah."
"10212","10184 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bistam narrated, Said ibn Shaqiq al-Jahdari narrated, Shubah narrated, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give the salutation to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen."
"10213","10185 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Jabir, from Amir, from Masruq, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give the salutation to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek appeared: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah."
"10214","10186 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to me, Abu Said al-Muaddib narrated, from Zakariyya, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: Of the things I have forgotten, I have not forgotten the salutation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer to his right and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah."
"10215","10187 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih narrated, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give the salutation to his right and to his left."
"10216","10188 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, my father narrated to me, Abu Hanifah narrated, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give the salutation to his right and to his left."
"10217","10189 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) giving the salutation to his right and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah."
"10218","10190 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Rabi ibn Tariq narrated, Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim narrated, Sulayman al-Amash narrated to me, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from al-Aswad and Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer; when he finished we said: O Messenger of Allah, has something new happened in the prayer? He said: No; I am only a human like you, so when I forget, remind me. Then he faced the qiblah with them, said the takbir and they said the takbir, then prostrated and they prostrated, then said the takbir and prostrated and they prostrated, then gave the salutation to his right and to his left."
"10219","10191 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Said ibn Abi al-Rabi al-Samman narrated, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Walid ibn Madan narrated, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh and Abu Wail, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: It is as if I am looking at the whiteness of the cheeks of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) giving the salutation to his right: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah."
"10220","10192 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated, Ubayd ibn Amr narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, he said: I prayed with Ali and Abdullah, and I saw them giving the salutation to their rights and to their lefts: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. And he claimed that they prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gave the salutation to his right: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen from both sides."
"10221","10193 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Abu Mamar, from Abdullah: It was said to him: A man in Makkah gives two salutations. He said: How did he pick that up?"
"10222","10194 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Dinar narrated, Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated, from Abd al-Salam ibn Harb, from Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from al-Hakam, from Abu Mamar, from Abdullah, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) giving two salutations."
"10223","10195 - Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi narrated to us, Sulayman al-Shadhakuni narrated, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, from Ubaydah, from Ibrahim, from Abu Mamar, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give the salutation to his right and to his left."
"10224","10196 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatiraniyy narrated to us, Ali ibn Abi Talib al-Bazzaz narrated, Musa ibn Umayr narrated, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fortify your wealth with zakah, treat your sick with charity, and prepare supplication for calamity."
"10225","10197 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Suhayb al-Nadr ibn Said ibn al-Nadr ibn Shubrumah al-Harithi narrated, Musa ibn Umayr narrated, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any man whom Allah has given knowledge and he conceals it, Allah will bridle him on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire."
"10226","10198 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar al-Attar al-Basri narrated, Abd al-Hamid al-Zarrad, meaning Ibn al-Hasan al-Hilali, narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When it is a fasting day of one of you, let him not be obscene nor ignorant; if someone acts ignorantly toward him, let him say: I am fasting. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: Fasting is Mine, and I reward for it. The fasting person has two joys: a joy on the day he meets his Lord, and a joy at his breaking of the fast; and the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."
"10227","10199 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Nasr ibn Bab narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks, asking while he is self-sufficient, it will come on the Day of Resurrection as scratches on his face. Charity is not lawful for one who has fifty dirhams, or its equivalent in gold."
"10228","10200 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated, al-Fudayl ibn Maysarah narrated, from Abu Hariz, that Ibrahim narrated to him, that al-Aswad ibn Yazid narrated to him, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever gives two loans will have the reward of one of them as if he had given it in charity."
"10229","10201 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought captives, and he would give each household together, disliking to separate them."
"10230","10202 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated, Shayban narrated, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: We used to perform ablution from touching the leper."
"10231","10203 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Waki narrated, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Hujayr al-Thalabi, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, he said: Seek it on the night of the seventeenth, for it is the morning of the Day of Criterion, the day the two hosts met."
"10232","10204 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, (H) and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from Kathir ibn Mudrik al-Ashjai, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: The measure of the noon prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in summer was three feet to five feet, and in winter five feet to seven feet."
"10233","10205 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abbad ibn Ahmad al-Arzami narrated, my uncle narrated, from his father, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu al-Safar, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from misappropriation; and begin with those you support."
"10234","10206 - al-Husayn ibn Jafar al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us, Ismail ibn al-Khalil al-Khazzaz narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There will be rulers who kill the prayer and strangle it toward the east of the dead; it is the prayer of one worse than a donkey, and the prayer of one who finds no escape. Whoever among you reaches that time, let him make the prayer at its time, and make your prayer with them supererogatory."
"10235","10207 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Ata al-Khuzai narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that any of the children of Adam castrate himself."
"10236","10208 - Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran al-Naqid narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated, Yusuf ibn Hawshab al-Shaybani narrated, Abu Yazid al-Awar narrated, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world shall not pass away until a man of my household rules, whose name corresponds to my name."
"10237","10209 - Abu Habib Yahya ibn Nafi al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Yahya ibn Ayyub reported, Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr narrated, from al-Amash, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was held back one night, being with one of his family or his wives, and did not come to us for the last evening prayer until the night had gone. He came to us while some of us were praying and some lying down, and he gave us glad tidings, saying: None of the People of the Book prays this prayer. Then there was sent down: {They are not equal; among the People of the Book is an upright community reciting the verses of Allah during the night while they prostrate}."
"10238","10210 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Irs al-Misri narrated to us, Wahb Allah ibn Rizq Abu Hurayrah al-Misri narrated, Bishr ibn Bakr narrated, al-Awzai narrated to me, Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah al-Azdi narrated to me, Zirr ibn Hubaysh narrated to me, he said: When people objected to the conduct of al-Walid ibn Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt, the people rushed to Abd Allah ibn Masud, so Abd Allah ibn Masud said to them: Be patient, for the tyranny of a ruler for fifty years is better than chaos for a month. That is because I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: People must have a rule, righteous or wicked. As for the righteous, it is just in distribution, and it is distributed among you so it reaches you equally; as for the wicked, the believer is tested therein. And wicked rule is better than chaos. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is chaos? He said: Killing and lying."
"10239","10211 - al-Husayn ibn Abd Allah al-Kharaqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mirdas al-Ansari narrated, Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Sayyar Abu al-Hakam, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about these two surahs, and he said: It was said to me, so I said it; so say as I said."
"10240","10212 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Zakariyya ibn Abd Allah al-Suhbani narrated, from his father, from Zirr, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praising the Nakha, until I wished I were a man of the Nakha."
"10241","10213 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The world shall not pass away until Allah sends a man of my household, whose name corresponds to my name, and whose father's name corresponds to my father's name."
"10242","10214 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dahir al-Razi narrated, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Quddus narrated, from al-Amash, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour shall not rise until a man of my household rules, whose name corresponds to my name; he will fill the earth with justice and equity just as it was filled with wrongdoing and tyranny."
"10243","10215 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abd Allah al-Mawsili narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The nights and days shall not pass away until a man of my household rules, whose name corresponds to my name."
"10244","10216 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu Shihab Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Kinani narrated, Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If nothing remained of the world but a night, a man of the household of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would rule in it."
"10245","10217 - al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Dallal al-Kufi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sini narrated, Abd Allah ibn Hakim ibn Jubayr narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world shall not pass away until a man of my household rules, whose name corresponds to my name."
"10246","10218 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, (H) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated, (H) and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated, my father narrated, all of them from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world shall not end until a man of my household rules the Arabs, whose name corresponds to my name. And the wording is from the hadith of Musaddad."
"10247","10219 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hamid ibn Yahya al-Balkhi narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The days and nights shall not pass away until a man of my household rules, whose name corresponds to my name; he will fill the earth with justice just as it was filled with tyranny and wrongdoing."
"10248","10220 - Umar ibn Ibrahim al-Baghdadi and Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Khalid al-Attar narrated, Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar narrated, Shubah narrated, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world shall not pass away until a man of my household governs, filling the earth with equity and justice just as it was filled with wrongdoing and tyranny; his name corresponds to my name."
"10249","10221 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated, Asim reported to me, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The world shall not end until a man of my household governs, whose name corresponds to my name."
"10250","10222 - al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Mujashii al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub al-Kirmani narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated, from Zaidah, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If nothing remained of the world but a day, Allah would lengthen that day until Allah sends therein a man of me, or of my household, whose name corresponds to my name, and whose father's name corresponds to my father's name."
"10251","10223 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated, Umar ibn Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: The world shall not pass away, or the days shall not end, until a man of my household rules the Arabs, whose name corresponds to my name."
"10252","10224 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi narrated, Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If nothing remained of the world but a night, Allah would lengthen that night until a man of my household rules, whose name corresponds to my name, and whose father's name corresponds to my father's name; he will fill it with equity and justice just as it was filled with wrongdoing and tyranny."
"10253","10225 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated, Yusuf ibn Hawshab narrated, Wasit ibn al-Harith narrated, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world shall not pass away until a man of my household rules, whose name corresponds to my name; he will fill the earth with equity and justice just as it was filled with tyranny and wrongdoing."
"10254","10226 - Yahya ibn Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Jarir ibn Abd Allah al-Bajali al-Kufi narrated to us, Jafar ibn Ali ibn Khalid ibn Jarir narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, he said: I asked Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, saying: O Abu Bakr, did you mention, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world shall not pass away until a man of my household rules, whose name corresponds to my name? He said: Yes."
"10255","10227 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jammal al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Amir ibn Ibrahim narrated, my father narrated, from Yaqub al-Qummi, from Sad ibn al-Husayn, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man of my household will govern the affair of this ummah at the end of its time, whose name corresponds to my name."
"10256","10227/2 - Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Muslim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated, Abu Ghassan al-Mismai narrated, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated, my father narrated to me, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The days shall not pass away until a man of my household rules, whose name corresponds to my name; he will fill the earth with equity and justice just as it was filled with wrongdoing and tyranny."
"10257","10228 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Subayh narrated, Ismail ibn Aban narrated, Abd Allah ibn Muslim al-Mulai narrated, from Abu al-Jahhaf, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The days and nights shall not pass away until a man of my household rules."
"10258","10229 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Wasil ibn Abd al-Ala narrated, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated, from Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Shubrumah, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man of my household will come forth, whose name corresponds to my name, and whose character is my character; he will fill it with justice and equity just as it was filled with wrongdoing and tyranny."
"10259","10230 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Amr al-Anqazi narrated, Tamim ibn al-Jad narrated, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mulai, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The days and nights shall not pass away, even if nothing remained of the world but a day, until Allah sends a man of my ummah whose name corresponds to my name."
"10260","10231 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated, (H) and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih al-Ijli narrated, both saying: Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated, Shuayb ibn Khalid narrated, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep refreshing the Quran, for it is wild; it escapes from men's chests faster than camels from their hobbles. Let none of you say: I forgot such-and-such verse; rather, he was made to forget."
"10261","10232 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting the thirteenth, the fourteenth, and the fifteenth is the fasting of the year and its breaking."
"10262","10233 - al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Dallal al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast Mondays and Thursdays."
"10263","10234 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Haytham al-Muadhdhin narrated, my father narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cheats us is not of us, and scheming and deception are in the Fire."
"10264","10235 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Said Abu Umar al-Darir al-Kufi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the pre-dawn meal, for there is blessing in the pre-dawn meal."
"10265","10236 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The woman who buries alive and the girl buried alive are in the Fire."
"10266","10237 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Badr were three hundred."
"10267","10238 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Nuaym Dirar ibn Surad narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: We were forbidden from prayer at sunrise and at sunset."
"10268","10239 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Ijli narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: What is wealth? He said: Despair of what is in people's hands."
"10269","10240 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There are no two Muslims between whom two of their children die but Allah will admit them to Paradise by virtue of His mercy to them."
"10270","10241 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Amr al-Hanafi narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The first to shoot an arrow in the path of Allah was Sad."
"10271","10242 - Jafar ibn Ahmad al-Shami al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Said ibn Walid narrated, from Nuh ibn Abi Maryam, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: As for me, I prostrate on seven bones, and I do not tuck up hair or garment."
"10272","10243 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Harmalah al-Abdi narrated, Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Bakr, I saw myself last night at a well, drawing water; then you came and drew, though you were weak, and may Allah forgive you. Then Umar came and it turned into a large bucket, and the people watered their camels around it."
"10273","10244 - al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Dallal al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Marry virgins, for they are sweeter in mouths, more productive in wombs, and more content with little."
"10274","10245 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Hashim ibn Muhammad al-Rabai narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: {Say: He is Allah, the One} equals a third of the Quran."
"10275","10246 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzaz narrated to us, both saying: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated, Rayhan ibn Said narrated, Ararah ibn al-Birind narrated, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When three gather, two shall not converse privately to the exclusion of the third, for that grieves him."
"10276","10247 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzaz narrated to us, both saying: Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated, Rayhan ibn Said narrated, Ararah ibn al-Birind narrated, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman shall not describe a woman to her husband as if he is looking at her."
"10277","10248 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzaz narrated to us, both saying: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated, Rayhan ibn Said narrated, Ararah narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seizes a Muslim's wealth by his oath will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection while He is angry with him."
"10278","10249 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, both saying: Said ibn Abi al-Rabi al-Samman narrated, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Walid ibn Madan narrated, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in witr: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High}, and {Say: O disbelievers}, and {Say: He is Allah, the One}."
"10279","10250 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, both saying: Said ibn Abi al-Rabi narrated, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Walid ibn Madan narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in the two rakahs before the morning prayer: {Say: O disbelievers}, and {Say: He is Allah, the One}."
"10280","10251 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, both saying: Said ibn Abi al-Rabi narrated, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Walid ibn Man narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two rakahs after Maghrib: {Say: O disbelievers}, and {Say: He is Allah, the One}."
"10281","10252 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Khalil al-Khushani narrated, Ayyub ibn Hassan al-Harashi narrated, from Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, from Aban, meaning al-Atta, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, that he narrated to him, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: A caller is sent at the time of every prayer, saying: O children of Adam, rise and extinguish what you have kindled against yourselves. They rise, purify themselves, their sins fall from their eyes, and they pray, and they are forgiven what is between them. Then they kindle in between that. When the first prayer comes, he calls: O children of Adam, rise and extinguish what you have kindled against yourselves. They rise, purify themselves, and pray, and they are forgiven what is between them. When Asr comes, the like of that; when Maghrib comes, the like of that; when the night prayer comes, the like of that; then they sleep having been forgiven. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So one sets out in the night toward good, and one sets out toward evil."
"10282","10253 - al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated, Abd Rabbihi ibn Maymun al-Nahhas narrated, from al-Rabi ibn Hizyan, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"10283","10254 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Muhriz ibn Salamah narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Arfajah ibn Abd al-Wahid, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: We used to call it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the Preventer; it is a surah in the Book of Allah: whoever recites it every night has done much and well."
"10284","10255 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated, my father narrated, from Yazid ibn Sinan, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is as if I am looking at Musa in this valley, entering ihram between two Qatawani cloaks."
"10285","10256 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, took Ibrahim as a close friend, and your companion is the close friend of Allah; and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the master of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection. Then he recited: {It may be that your Lord will raise you to a praised station}."
"10286","10257 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Buhlul al-Anbari narrated, Muhammad al-Sulami narrated, from Musa ibn Matir, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: On the day of Badr, when they brought the captives, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Abu Bakr and said: What do you think about these? He said: O Messenger of Allah, your people; if you kill them they will enter the Fire, and if you take ransom for them, whoever becomes Muslim will be a support for us, and whoever refuses, we take his ransom. He said: What do you think, O Umar? He said: I think you should present them and strike their necks; these are the leaders of disbelief. By Allah, they were not content to expel us until they were the first of the Arabs to raid us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Bakr, your likeness is that of Ibrahim, peace be upon him, when he said: {So whoever follows me is of me, and whoever disobeys me, then You are Forgiving, Merciful}. As for you, O Umar, your likeness is that of Nuh when he said: {My Lord, leave not upon the earth any dweller of the disbelievers}."
"10287","10258 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: On the day of Badr, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the captives and said: What do you think? Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, they denied you and expelled you; strike their necks. Abd Allah ibn Rawahah said: O Messenger of Allah, you are in a valley of abundant firewood, so kindle a fire and cast them into it. Al-Abbas said: May Allah cut your kinship. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, your kin, your root, and your people; pardon them, and Allah will save them through you from the Fire. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went in; some said: The right view is what Abu Bakr said, and some said: The right view is what Umar said. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and said: What do you say about these two men? Their likeness is that of brothers of theirs who came before them. Nuh said: {My Lord, leave not upon the earth any dweller of the disbelievers}. Musa said: {Our Lord, obliterate their wealth}. Isa said: {If You punish them, they are Your servants; and if You forgive them, You are the Mighty, the Wise}. Ibrahim said: {So whoever follows me is of me, and whoever disobeys me, then You are Forgiving, Merciful}. Allah strengthens the hearts of men through Him until they are harder than stones, and softens the hearts of men through Him until they are softer than softness. You are in need, and none of them shall return except with a ransom or a strike of the neck. Abdullah said: I said: Except Suhayl ibn Bayda. Abdullah said: I had heard him mention Islam, so he fell silent. I kept looking at the sky, wondering when stones would fall upon me; I said: I put speech forward before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until he said: Except Suhayl ibn Bayda."
"10288","10259 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came with the captives, he consulted the people about them. Abd Allah ibn Jahsh said: Enemies of Allah; they denied you, harmed you, expelled you, and fought you, while you are in a valley of abundant firewood, so gather much firewood for them and kindle a fire upon them. And he mentioned the like of the hadith of Zaidah, except that he put Abd Allah ibn Jahsh in place of Abd Allah ibn Rawahah; and the correct view is Abd Allah ibn Jahsh."
"10289","10260 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatiraniyy narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated, Hafs ibn Abi Dawud al-Asadi narrated, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abd Allah, from his father, he said: On the day of Badr, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took seventy men captive. He gathered his companions and said to them: Advise me about them. Abd Allah ibn Jahsh spoke, and he mentioned the like of it."
"10290","10261 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated: I found in the book of my uncle Umar ibn Hafs, in his handwriting, from his father, from Misar, Amr ibn Murrah narrated to me, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would find a man's shoulder out of line with his companion's shoulder, so he would straighten them, saying: Do not differ, lest your hearts differ."
"10291","10262 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated, (H) and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated, both saying: Mihran al-Razi narrated, from Abu Sinan, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray witr, O people of the Quran. A bedouin said: What is the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying? He said: You are not of its people."
"10292","10263 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, Israil narrated to me, from Ali ibn Badhimah, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abd Allah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray witr, O people of the Quran."
"10293","10264 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated, from his father, from al-Amash, from Ali ibn Badhimah, from Abu Ubaydah, he said: Abd Allah ibn Masud said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Children of Israil engaged in sins, their reciters and scholars forbade them what they were doing, but they disobeyed them, so they mixed with them in their livelihoods; then He struck the hearts of some of them against others. Then He cursed them upon the tongues of Dawud and Isa son of Maryam. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat up, having been reclining, then said: Nay, by the One in whose hand is my soul, until you bend them forcefully to the truth."
"10294","10265 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Ismail ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated, Sharik narrated, from Ali ibn Badhimah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the Children of Israil took to sins, their scholars forbade them but they did not desist, so they sat with them and kept company with them; so Allah struck the hearts of some of them against others. Then he said: {Cursed were those who disbelieved among the Children of Israil}, the verse."
"10295","10266 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Muammil ibn Ihab narrated, Malik ibn Suayr narrated, Misar narrated, from Ali ibn Badhimah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"10296","10267 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated, Jafar ibn Ziyad narrated, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you shall enjoin right, forbid wrong, seize the wrongdoer by the hand, bend him to the truth forcibly, or Allah will set the hearts of some of you against others and curse you as He cursed them."
"10297","10268 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated, Abu Shihab al-Hannat narrated, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Salim meaning al-Aftas, from Abu Ubaydah, from Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those before you, when one of them did a sin, the one who forbade forbade him by way of excuse; then the next day he sat with him, ate with him and drank with him, as if he had not seen him in sin yesterday. When Allah saw that of them, He set the hearts of some of them against others, then cursed them on the tongue of their prophet Dawud and Isa son of Maryam, for they disobeyed and transgressed. By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, you shall enjoin right, forbid wrong, seize the wrongdoer by the hands, bend him to the truth forcibly, or Allah will set the hearts of some of you against others, then curse you as He cursed them. Khalaf said: Ta'turunahu means you coerce him."
"10298","10269 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, Israil informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: They were made to look few in our eyes on the day of Badr, until I said to my companion beside me: How many do you think they are, do you think seventy? He said: I think a hundred; until we seized one of them and asked him, and he said: We were a thousand."
"10299","10270 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani, Abdan ibn Ahmad, and Ali ibn Bistam al-Zafarani narrated to us, they said: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: We never heard one pleading for his right pleading more urgently than Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Badr; he kept saying: O Allah, I plead with You for what You promised me; O Allah, if this band perishes, You will not be worshipped. Then he turned, his face as if the moon, and said: As if I am looking at the places where the people will fall this evening."
"10300","10271 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Amir ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from al-Numan ibn Abd al-Salam, from Isa ibn al-Dahhak, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"10301","10272 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bayan narrated, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated, from Sharik, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the fear prayer; he lined a row behind him and a row facing the enemy, prayed a unit with them, then the row next to him stepped back and stood where those facing the enemy were, and those advanced and prayed a unit behind him, then he gave salam with them; then those behind him stood and prayed a unit, then those advanced and stood in the place of these and prayed a unit."
"10302","10273 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Quran was sent down upon seven modes; whoever recites upon one of them should not shift to another out of aversion to it."
"10303","10274 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated, Yazid ibn Ata narrated, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a donkey named Ufayr."
"10304","10275 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Haytham al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated, Mamar narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, that some people came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Our companion is ill, shall we cauterize him? He was silent a while, then said: If you wish, cauterize him, and if you wish, crush for him medicine to snuff."
"10305","10276 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from misappropriated spoils."
"10306","10277 - Ali ibn Muhammad al-Ansana'i al-Misri narrated to us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Salim informed me, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abdullah ibn Ali, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have mercy on those on earth, He in heaven will have mercy on you."
"10307","10278 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Shubah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked: Who are the noblest of people? He said: Yusuf son of Yaqub son of Ishaq, the sacrificed of Allah."
"10308","10279 - Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Hammad al-Barbari narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated, Yahya ibn Adam narrated, Sharik narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Aishah when she was six years old, consummated with her when she was nine, and died when she was eighteen."
"10309","10280 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Thawban ibn Said ibn Arubah narrated, Ali ibn Abis narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us, when we began prayer, to say: Glory be to You O Allah and with Your praise, blessed is Your name, exalted is Your grandeur, and there is no god but You."
"10310","10281 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mualla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated, Wuhayb narrated, from Mamar, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The one who repents from sin is like one with no sin."
"10311","10282 - Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated, Ali ibn Abis narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Kanud, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went to his bed, said: O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the day You resurrect Your servants."
"10312","10283 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we were kept from the noon, afternoon, sunset and night prayers; it weighed heavily on us, and we said: We are with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and in the cause of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Bilal, who called the iqamah; we prayed each prayer with an iqamah. He said: There is no band on earth remembering Allah besides you."
"10313","10284 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, Zaidah narrated, from Misar, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The sitting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the two units was as if on hot stones."
"10314","10285 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, Shubah narrated, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, he said: I heard Abu Ubaydah narrating from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when in the two units, was as if on hot stones; I say: until he stands, and he says: until he stands."
"10315","10286 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Azhar ibn Marwan al-Raqqashi narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, Abdullah ibn al-Rabi ibn Khuthaym narrated, Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah narrated: al-Rabi ibn Khuthaym, when he entered upon Abdullah, needed no permission until each had finished with the other. He said: Abdullah said: O Abu Yazid, had the Messenger of Allah seen you he would have loved you; whenever I see you I remember the humble."
"10316","10287 - Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Missisi and al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, they said: al-Musayyab ibn Wadih narrated, Yusuf ibn Asbat narrated, from Sufyan, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever builds beyond what suffices him will be burdened with carrying it on his neck on the Day of Resurrection."
"10317","10288 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Ismail ibn Isa al-Attar narrated, Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated, from Asim, from Abu al-Uryan, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in al-Najm, he and the polytheists together."
"10318","10289 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, al-Masudi informed us, from Said ibn Amr ibn Jad, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the Night of Decree, and said: Which of you remembers the reddish clouds? Abdullah said: I do, may my father and mother be ransom for you O Messenger of Allah, when the moon rose, that being the night of the twenty-seventh."
"10319","10290 - al-Sari ibn Sahl al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Rashid narrated, Mujjaah ibn al-Zubayr narrated, from Qatadah, from Uqbah ibn Abd al-Ghafir, from Abu Ubaydah, from Ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be truly modest before Allah. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we are modest, praise be to Allah. He said: Not that; rather whoever is truly modest before Allah, let him guard the head and what it contains, the belly and what it holds, remember death and decay; whoever desires the Hereafter abandons the adornment of the world; whoever does that has been truly modest before Allah."
"10320","10291 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Idris al-Hulwani narrated, Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Qatadah, from Abu Mijlaz, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to al-Mundhir ibn Sawa: Whoever prays our prayer, faces our qiblah, and eats our slaughtered meat, that is the Muslim; he has the protection of Allah and the protection of the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10321","10292 - Abu Abd al-Malik Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, al-Salt ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Zubaydi narrated, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from Qatadah, from Abu Mijlaz, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you points a spear at a man, if its tip is at the hollow of his throat and he says: There is no god but Allah, let him lift the spear from him."
"10322","10293 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Layth narrated to me, al-Ashjai narrated, from Sufyan, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment; they were struck down, and they said: When you meet your people, convey from us that we met our Lord, were pleased, and He was pleased with us."
"10323","10294 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Hamid ibn Yahya al-Balkhi narrated, Hafs ibn Salm narrated, Misar narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: Beware of testimonies; if you must do it, testify for a detachment the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent and they were struck down; it was revealed concerning them that: Convey from us to our people that we have met our Lord, and He is pleased with us and has contented us."
"10324","10295 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Masud, from his father, he said: Allah the Exalted sent His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to bring a man into Paradise; he entered a church, and there were Jews reading the Torah; when they came to the description of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they held back. In its corner was a sick man. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you hold back? The sick man said: They came to the description of a prophet and held back. The sick man came crawling until he took the Torah and read it until he came to the description of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his community, and said: This is your description and your community's description; I bear witness there is no god but Allah and you are the Messenger of Allah. Then he died. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prepare your brother for burial."
"10325","10296 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Hasan ibn Atiyyah narrated, from Qays, from Abu Sad al-Baqqal, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: We had no festival except in the forenoon, and I saw us gathering with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the shade of al-Hatim."
"10326","10297 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Wadih al-Assal al-Misri and Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, they said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu Ishaq, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade slapping cheeks and tearing garments."
"10327","10298 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Nafi narrated, al-Fadl ibn al-Ala narrated, Ashath ibn Sawwar narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Masruq, he said: Abdullah said: You were commanded to uphold four: upholding prayer, giving zakat, and: Establish Hajj and Umrah to the House; Hajj is the greater pilgrimage, Umrah the lesser pilgrimage."
"10328","10299 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Israil, al-Masudi, Abu al-Ahwas and Zuhayr narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Masruq, he said: You were commanded in the Book of Allah with four: upholding prayer, giving zakat, Hajj, and Umrah to the House. And Ibn Masud was not mentioned."
"10329","10300 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated, and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, they said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from Abu Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Bilal, who had a heap of dates, and said: What is this, O Bilal? He said: O Messenger of Allah, for you and your guests. He said: Do you not fear it may become a vapor of Fire? Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear decrease from the Lord of the Throne."
"10330","10301 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from al-Amash, from Muslim Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking one another's necks."
"10331","10302 - Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Hammad, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when bowing or prostrating, said: Glory be to You and with Your praise, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You."
"10332","10303 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, Hammam narrated, from Asim, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two eyes commit adultery, the two hands commit adultery, and the two feet commit adultery."
"10333","10304 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Ibn Jurayj informed me, from Ayyub ibn Hani, from Masruq ibn al-Ajda, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had forbidden you drinks in vessels; indeed no vessel makes anything unlawful; every intoxicant is unlawful."
"10334","10305 - Abu Masud Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni al-Tustari narrated to us, Ismail ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated, Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Hashimi narrated, Abd al-Nur ibn Abdullah al-Mismai narrated, from Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah commanded me to marry Fatimah to Ali, may Allah be pleased with them."
"10335","10306 - al-Hasan ibn Alluyah al-Qattan narrated to us, Abbad ibn Musa al-Khuttali narrated, Ismail ibn Jafar narrated, from Habib ibn Hassan, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The severest of people in punishment on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers."
"10336","10307 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ruzayq al-Rasibi narrated, Khalid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a wicked oath to cut off thereby the property of a Muslim man will meet Allah while He is angry with him."
"10337","10308 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Baghawi narrated, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated, from Sufyan, from Zubayd, from Abu Wail, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Reviling the Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."
"10338","10309 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Aqil Yahya ibn Habib ibn Ismail ibn Abdullah ibn Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated, al-Fadl ibn Dalham narrated, from Ibn Sirin, Masruq ibn al-Ajda narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the woman who joins hair and the one joined, the tattooer and the tattooed."
"10339","10310 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, he said: We were sitting with Abdullah ibn Masud, and a man asked him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, did you ask your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) how many caliphs will rule this community? Ibn Masud said: None asked me about it since I came to Iraq before you; we asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Twelve, the number of the chiefs of the Children of Israil. The wording is of Hajjaj's hadith."
"10340","10311 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Sharik narrated, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The millstone of Islam will turn in the year thirty-five; if they perish, by the path of those who perished, and if they survive, they remain seventy years."
"10341","10312 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Hamid ibn Yahya al-Balkhi narrated, Muhammad ibn Manadhir the poet narrated, Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Kufi narrated to me, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at the slain on the day of Badr, he said to Abu Bakr: Had Abu Talib been alive, he would know our swords have taken their due; and of that Abu Talib says, Ibn Manadhir said, both alike, they say: Halahil and Jalajil."
"10342","10313 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No judge judging among people but will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection with an angel holding his nape until he stands him over Hell; then he raises his head to heaven; if Allah says: Cast him, his fall is forty autumns."
"10343","10314 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated, my father narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, strengthen Islam with Umar ibn al-Khattab or Abu Jahl ibn Hisham. Allah made His Messenger's supplication for Umar ibn al-Khattab; Islam was built upon him and idols demolished through him."
"10344","10315 - Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Burayq al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Said ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated, Yahya ibn Wadih Abu Tumaylah narrated, from Abu Hamzah, from Jabir, from Amir, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me, let him take a house in the Fire."
"10345","10316 - Khayr ibn Arafah al-Misri narrated to us, Urwah ibn Marwan al-Raqqi narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Reviling the Muslim is wickedness, fighting him is disbelief, and the sanctity of his property is like the sanctity of his blood."
"10346","10317 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, Israil informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked to supplicate three times and seek forgiveness three times."
"10347","10318 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to me, and al-Husayn ibn Jafar al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated, they said: Sharik narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, I think from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: He is Allah, the One, is a third of the Quran."
"10348","10319 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, he said: I heard Abdullah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: To proceed."
"10349","10320 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman al-Ashall narrated, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood over the people of the pit and said: O people of the pit, have you found what your Lord promised true? I have found what my Lord promised me true. They said: O Messenger of Allah, do they hear? He said: You do not hear what I say better than they, but today they do not answer."
"10350","10321 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani and al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us, they said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The first group to enter Paradise, their faces as the light of the moon on the night of full moon; the second group of the color of the fairest brilliant star in the sky; for each man of them two wives of the wide-eyed maidens; upon each wife seventy garments; the marrow of their shanks seen from behind their flesh and garments as red drink is seen in a white glass."
"10351","10322 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, Israil informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge from five: cowardice, miserliness, evil old age, the trial of the breast, and the punishment of the grave."
"10352","10323 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Shabab al-Usfuri narrated, Abu Attab al-Dallal narrated, Jarir ibn Ayyub narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning His saying: On the day the earth is changed to other than the earth, he said: A white earth as if silver, in which no unlawful blood was shed, nor disobedience done."
"10353","10324 - al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi Yaqub al-Kirmani narrated, Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah's houses on earth are the mosques; it is a due upon Allah to honor whoever visits Him in them."
"10354","10325 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated, Sharik narrated, from Asim, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Masud, raised, that he said: The best of you is he who recites the Quran and teaches it."
"10355","10326 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Abyad ibn Aban narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us: When one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; when he says that, let whoever is with him say: May Allah have mercy on you; when he says it, let him say: May Allah forgive me and you."
"10356","10327 - Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated, Amr ibn Uthman al-Jufi narrated, my uncle Abu Muslim Ubaydullah ibn Said al-Jufi, guide of al-Amash, narrated, from al-Amash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in an upper room as if a bath chamber, sleeping on a mat that had marked his side, and I wept. He said: What makes you weep, O Abdullah? I said: O Messenger of Allah, Khosrow and Caesar tread on brocade, silk and silk brocade, while you sleep on this mat that has marked your side. He said: Do not weep, O Abdullah; theirs is the world, ours the Hereafter. What have I to do with the world; my likeness and the world's is but as a rider who alighted under a tree, then moved on and left it."
"10357","10328 - Jabrun ibn Isa al-Muqri in Egypt narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Hafari al-Muqri narrated, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated, from al-Amash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever's heart drinks love of the world clings to it with three: unending toil, greed never reaching sufficiency, hope never reaching its end. The world is seeker and sought: whoever seeks the world, the Hereafter seeks him until death comes and takes him; whoever seeks the Hereafter, the world seeks him until he takes his full provision of it."
"10358","10329 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Ahwal narrated, Abu Ubaydah ibn Man narrated, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abdullah, he said: The people of a prophethood never perish until adultery and usury appear."
"10359","10330 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated, Ayyub Abu al-Jamal narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The camel in sacrifice is for ten."
"10360","10331 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Wasiti narrated, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Sharik informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No disease was placed on earth but a cure was made for it; whoever knows it knows it, whoever is ignorant of it is ignorant of it."
"10361","10332 - Ishaq ibn Khalawayh al-Wasiti narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Ziyad ibn Abdullah al-Bakkai narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A day's food is a duty, two days' food is a sunna, the third day's food is showing off; whoever shows off, Allah exposes him."
"10362","10333 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hafs al-Tumani narrated, Yahya ibn Kathir narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The expiation of a gathering is for the servant to say: Glory be to You O Allah and with Your praise, I bear witness there is no god but Allah, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You."
"10363","10334 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abidah, from Abdullah, he said: A comer of the People of the Book came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, Allah places the heavens on a finger, the mountains on a finger, the trees on a finger, the water and soil on a finger, then says: I am the King. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until his molars appeared, then said: And they did not esteem Allah His true esteem."
"10364","10335 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Sufyan, Mansur and Sulayman narrated to me, from Ibrahim, from Abidah, from Abdullah, that a Jew came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Allah holds the heavens on a finger; he mentioned the like of it."
"10365","10336 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Said al-Wasiti narrated, Dawud ibn Rashid al-Wasiti narrated, Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated, from Abu Hashim al-Rummani, from Ibrahim, from Abidah, from Abdullah, he said: A rabbi of the rabbis came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah the Mighty and Majestic will place the heavens on this, mankind on this, the mountains on this, and the earth on this. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and recited: And they did not esteem Allah His true esteem, to His saying: above what they associate."
"10366","10337 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abidah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of this community are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them; then a people will come whose oaths precede their testimonies and their testimonies their oaths."
"10367","10338 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Nahwi Abu Muawiyah informed us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abidah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which people are best? He said: My generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them; then a people will come whose one's testimony precedes his oath and his oath his testimony."
"10368","10339 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abidah al-Salmani, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The last to exit the Fire and enter Paradise is a man crawling; it is said to him: Enter Paradise, and it appears to him full. He says: My Lord, it is full. It is said to him: Enter, for you are ten times the world, or the like of the world ten times. He says: You are the King, do You jest with me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until he showed ..."
"10369","10340 - al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim ibn Marzuq al-Razi narrated, my father Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to me, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from Abidah al-Salmani, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you seen the last of the people of Paradise to enter and the last of the people of the Fire to exit? A man scorched by the Fire; his Lord passes by him and he says: My Lord, take me out of this Fire to the shade of a tree. When he finds relief, he looks at a tree of Paradise and says: My Lord. He went out, having no deed to lift him, crawling until he came to them and found no abode in it for him. He returned to his Lord the Mighty and Majestic and said: My Lord, I found no abode in it. He said: Go, for you are the like of the world and ten its likes. He said: That is the least of the people of Paradise in share. He said: Do You mock me while You are my Lord? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until his molars and grinders appeared."
"10370","10341 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Mahfuz ibn Nasr al-Hamdani narrated, Abu Maryam Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim narrated, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Ibrahim, from Abidah al-Salmani, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out for his need; I brought him water. He said: Who commanded you with this? I said: None commanded me. He said: You did well, glad tidings of Paradise to you. Then Ali came and he gave him glad tidings of Paradise."
"10371","10342 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Nuaym Dirar ibn Surad narrated, Yahya ibn Yala al-Aslami narrated, Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated, from his father, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, from Abidah, from Abdullah, he said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: A man of the people of Paradise will come upon you. Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, entered, greeted, and ascended."
"10372","10343 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Dirar ibn Surad narrated, Yahya ibn Yala narrated, from Sharik, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, from Abidah, from Abdullah, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: A man of the people of Paradise will come upon you. Abu Bakr then Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, appeared."
"10373","10344 - Jafar ibn Ahmad al-Shami al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Mukhtar ibn Ghassan narrated, Talid ibn Sulayman narrated, from Abu al-Jahhaf, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, from Abidah, from Ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in a garden and said: A man of the people of Paradise will enter. Abu Bakr entered, then he said: A man of the people of Paradise will enter. Umar entered, then he said: A man of the people of Paradise will enter. Ali, may Allah be pleased with them, entered."
"10374","10345 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abidah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some poetry is wisdom, and some eloquence is magic."
"10375","10346 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to me, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some poetry is wisdom."
"10376","10347 - Umar ibn Ibrahim al-Baghdadi and Bakr ibn Muqbil al-Basri narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Malik ibn Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated, my uncle Amr ibn Khalifah narrated to me, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abidah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Keep the Quran in mind; it slips from men's breasts more violently than straying camels to their homes."
"10377","10348 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Ibn Masud, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah hears him who praises Him, he said: O Allah our Lord, to You is praise filling the heavens, filling the earth, filling whatever You will after, O Possessor of praise."
"10378","10349 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey; the people said: Let us camp for the night. He said: Who will wake us? I said: I will guard you and wake you. I slept and they slept; we woke only to the sun's heat on our heads. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the last of us; he stood, performed ablution with the people, prayed two units, then prayed Fajr."
"10379","10350 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Affan narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, al-Harith ibn Hasirah narrated, al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How would you be with a quarter of the people of Paradise yours and three quarters for the rest of people? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: How would you be with a third? They said: That is more. He said: How would you be with half? They said: That is more. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise are a hundred and twenty rows; you are eighty rows of them."
"10380","10351 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, al-Harith ibn Hasirah informed us, al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, from his father, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn; the people turned away from him, and I remained with him among eighty of the Emigrants and Helpers. We stepped back on our feet about eighty paces, and did not turn our backs; they are those upon whom Allah the Mighty and Majestic sent down tranquility. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was advancing on his mule; his mule swerved with him, and he leaned from the saddle. I hastened toward him and said: Rise up, may Allah raise you. He said: Hand me a handful of dust. He struck their faces with it, and their eyes filled with dust. He said: Where are the Emigrants and Helpers? I said: Here they are. He said: Call out to them. I called out, and they came, swords in their right hands as if shooting stars; the polytheists turned their backs."
"10381","10352 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated, Abu Salamah ibn al-Juhani narrated, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim is ever struck by worry or grief and says: O Allah, I am Your servant, son of Your servant, son of Your maid; my forelock is in Your hand; Your judgment over me is executed; Your decree over me is just; I ask You by every name of Yours, by which You named Yourself, sent down in Your Book, taught to any of Your creation, or kept in the knowledge of the unseen with You, to make the Quran the spring of my heart, the light of my sight, the remover of my grief and the dispeller of my worry, but Allah removes his worry and replaces his grief with joy. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not learn these words? He said: Rather, whoever hears them should learn them."
"10382","10353 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Faydi narrated, Jabir ibn Nuh narrated, from al-Masudi, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let your house contain you, weep over remembrance of your sin, and hold your tongue."
"10383","10354 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Khalifah ibn Khayyat narrated, Umar ibn Ali narrated, Musa al-Juhani narrated to me, al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever forgets to mention Allah's name at the start of his food, let him say when he remembers: In the name of Allah at its start and end; he meets fresh food, and prevents the wicked what he would take of it."
"10384","10355 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Khalaf al-Wasiti narrated, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated, from Sharik, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill all snakes; whoever leaves them fearing their revenge is not of me."
"10385","10356 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The millstone of Islam will turn at the head of thirty-five, thirty-six, or thirty-seven; if they perish, by the path of those who perished, and if they remain, they remain seventy years."
"10386","10357 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi Hassan al-Anmati narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, Bukayr ibn Maruf narrated to me, from Muqatil ibn Hayyan, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ibn Masud. I said: At your service, thrice. He said: Do you know which handholds of faith are firmest? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Allegiance for Allah, love for Allah, hate for Allah. He said: O Ibn Masud. I said: At your service O Messenger of Allah. He said: Which believers are best? I said: O Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: When they know their religion, the best of them in deed. Then he said: O Ibn Masud, do you know which believers are most knowledgeable? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: When they differ, and he interlaced his fingers, the keenest of them on the truth, though his deed falls short, though he crawls crawling. Then he said: O Ibn Masud, did you know the Children of Israil split into seventy-two sects, of which only three sects were saved: a sect that stood among kings and tyrants calling to the religion of Isa; they were seized and sawn with saws, burned with fires, and endured until they met Allah. Then another group stood lacking strength, unable to uphold justice, so they joined the mountains, worshipping and monastic; they are those Allah mentioned saying: And monasticism they innovated, We did not prescribe it for them, but seeking Allah's pleasure, to: and many of them are wicked. A sect of them believed; they are those who believed and affirmed me, who observed it with true observance, and many of them are wicked, and they are those who did not believe in me, did not affirm me, did not observe it with true observance, and they are those Allah declared wicked."
"10387","10358 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Mindal ibn Ali narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to place his right hand over his left in prayer."
"10388","10359 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Jabir, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: When captives were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he gave the household all together, disliking to separate them."
"10389","10360 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated, from Hamzah al-Zayyat, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, he said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by, and people kept saying: This is the Messenger of Allah. A Jew said: If he is the Messenger of Allah, I shall ask him something; if a prophet, he will know it. He said: O Abu al-Qasim, tell me, is man created from the man's fluid or the woman's fluid? He said: The man's fluid is white and thick; from it are bones and sinews. The woman's fluid is yellow and thin; from it are blood and flesh."
"10390","10361 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafii narrated, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated, from Ibn Khuthaym, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rulers will come over you delaying prayer from its times and innovating novelties. He said: What shall I do if I reach them? He said: Do you ask me, son of Umm Abd, what to do? No obedience to one who disobeys Allah."
"10391","10362 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: We read upon Muhammad ibn Hafs ibn Umar al-Darir al-Muqri, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated, Huraym ibn Sufyan narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The glance is a poisoned arrow of Iblis's arrows; whoever abandons it out of fear of Me, I replace it with faith whose sweetness he finds in his heart."
"10392","10363 - Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Muthanna al-Juhani al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Khazzar narrated, Sayyar ibn Hatim narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw Ibrahim (peace be upon him) on the night I was taken by night; he said: O Muhammad, convey my greeting to your community and tell them Paradise is sweet of soil, sweet of water, level plains, its planting: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, Allah is greatest, and no power nor strength but by Allah."
"10393","10364 - Ishaq ibn Khalawayh al-Wasiti narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated, from al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: Two men of Juhaynah shared a boy; one freed him. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who made him liable for him. He had a small flock of nearly a hundred sheep; he sold it and paid his companion."
"10394","10365 - Muhammad ibn Salih al-Narsi narrated to us, Ali ibn Hassan al-Attar narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Man ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the two traders differ and the goods stand intact, the word is the seller's, or they rescind."
"10395","10366 - Ahmad ibn Rustah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated, al-Hakam ibn Ayyub narrated, from Zufar ibn al-Hudhayl, from Abu Hanifah, from Man ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: I never lied since I embraced Islam but one lie: I used to saddle for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); a man of Taif came and asked me: Which saddles are dearest to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: The Taifi with raised back, though he disliked it. When it was brought, he said: Who saddled this? They said: Your saddler. He said: Command Ibn Umm Abd to saddle. The saddling was returned to me."
"10396","10367 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abu Usamah narrated, from Misar, he said: Man ibn Abd al-Rahman brought out a book to me, and swore to me it was his father Abd al-Rahman's handwriting, and in it: Abdullah said: By Allah besides whom there is no god, I saw none harsher upon the hair-splitters than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10397","10368 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman ibn Atiq, from Talq ibn Habib, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed the hair-splitters are ruined."
"10398","10369 - Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi narrated to us, Hibban ibn Musa and Suwayd ibn Nasr narrated, they said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Misar, from Abu Bakr ibn Amr ibn Utbah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Masud, that al-Ashath ibn Qays entered upon Abdullah while he was eating on the day of Ashura; Abdullah said: It is but a day we used to fast before Ramadan."
"10399","10370 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Ayan al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Masud, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Children of Israil set a caliph over them; he stood praying in the moonlight above the Holy House, mentioned deeds he did, let himself down by a rope; in the morning the rope hung attached to the mosque, and he was gone. He went until he came to people on the seashore making bricks; he asked: How do you take wages for these bricks? They told him, and he made bricks with them, eating from his hand's work until prayer time came, when he purified himself and prayed. That worker was reported to their chief, who said: Among us is a man doing such and such. He sent for him, and he refused to come. Then he came riding his mount; when he saw him he fled, and he followed him and outran him, and said: Wait for me to speak a word to you. He stood until he spoke to him, and told him he had been a king fleeing in dread of his sin. He said: I shall join you in that. They worshipped Allah and asked Allah to make them both die together, and they died. Abdullah said: Had I been at Rumaylah of Egypt, I would show you their graves, as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) described."
"10400","10371 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Warraq narrated, Amr ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated, Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has servants He spares from killing; He lengthens their lives in good deeds, makes their provisions good, keeps them alive in well-being, takes their souls in well-being upon their beds, and gives them the ranks of martyrs."
"10401","10372 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ali ibn Nasr al-Jahdami narrated, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Yazid, master of pearls, narrated, my father narrated, Warqa narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Yahya ibn Jadah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram when his mount rose with him."
"10402","10373 - al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Ala al-Bushi al-Sanani narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated, al-Thawri informed us, from Salman al-Shaybani, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Masud, from his father, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he passed an ant village burned with fire, and said: None should punish with Allah's punishment."
"10403","10374 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Barra al-Sanani narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated, al-Thawri informed us, from Salman al-Shaybani, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he did not say: from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from his father."
"10404","10375 - al-Abbas and Ali ibn Said al-Raziyan narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Mumin narrated, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated, from Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Masud, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a red bird flying over his companions' heads, and said: Who frightened this? A man of the Ansar said: I took its eggs, or a chick. He commanded him to return it."
"10405","10376 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Khawwas al-Mawsili narrated, Sadan ibn Bishr al-Mawsili narrated, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"10406","10377 - Abdullah ibn Najiyah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Mahshar narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abu Sad al-Baqqal, from al-Shabi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the two sellers differ, the word is the seller's."
"10407","10378 - Abdan ibn Ahmad and al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Hammad ibn Numayr narrated, Husayn ibn Numayr narrated, from Husayn, from Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: None is more jealous than Allah the Mighty and Majestic, for He forbade indecencies; none loves praise more than Allah, for He praised Himself; none loves excuse more than Allah, for He excused to His creation; and none loves lauding more than Allah, for He lauded Himself."
"10408","10379 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Burjumi narrated, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated, Misar narrated, from Zubayd, from Murrah, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a guest; he sent to his wives seeking food with them, and found nothing with any of them. He said: O Allah, I ask You of Your bounty and mercy, for none owns them but You. A roasted sheep was gifted to him, and he said: This is of Allah's bounty, and we await mercy."
"10409","10380 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Tarif al-Bajali narrated, Mufaddal ibn Salih narrated, from Zubayd, from Murrah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Reviling the Muslim is wickedness, fighting him is disbelief."
"10410","10381 - Ahmad ibn Abi Yahya al-Hadrami al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Wasiti informed me, al-Mualla ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, Sufyan al-Thawri and Shubah narrated, from Zubayd, from Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray Fajr in brightness, for it is greater in reward."
"10411","10382 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Amr ibn Hisham Abu Umayyah al-Harrani narrated, Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated, from Sufyan, from Zubayd, from Murrah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The merit of night prayer over day prayer is as the merit of secret charity over open charity."
"10412","10383 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Murrah al-Hamdani, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Our Lord marvels at two men: a man who jumps from his bed and cover, between his beloved and family, to his prayer; Allah the Mighty and Majestic says to His angels: Look at My servant, who jumped from his bed and cover, from his beloved and family, to his prayer, desiring what is with Me and fearing what is with Me. And a man who raids in Allah's cause and is routed, knowing what is upon him in rout and what is for him in return; he returns until his blood is shed. Allah the Exalted says to His angels: Look at My servant, who returned desiring what is with Me and fearing what is with Me until his blood was shed."
"10413","10384 - Ishaq ibn Khalawayh al-Wasiti narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, al-Hakam ibn Zuhayr narrated, from al-Suddi, from Murrah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the people of the Fire were told: You will remain in the Fire the number of every pebble in the world, they would rejoice at it; and if the people of Paradise were told: You will remain in Paradise the number of every pebble in the world, they would grieve; but eternity was made for them."
"10414","10385 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, Muhammad ibn Talhah informed us, from Zubayd, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Qays ibn al-Sakan, he said: I was sitting with Abdullah ibn Masud on the day of Ashura, with a bowl of tharid by him; al-Ashath ibn Qays entered upon him, and he said: Will you not come near, O Abu Muhammad, to lunch? He said: Have you fasted this day? He said: This day we used to fast before Ramadan came down; when Ramadan came down, we fasted it and left the rest."
"10415","10386 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Muadh ibn Asad narrated, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated, Abd al-Ala ibn Abi al-Musawir narrated, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Qays ibn al-Sakan and Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah gathers the nations on the Day of Resurrection, then descends from His Throne to His Footstool, and His Footstool encompasses the heavens and the earth."
"10416","10387 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, Qanab ibn al-Muharrar ibn Qanab al-Bahili narrated, Said ibn Amir narrated, Shubah narrated, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three garments: a Sanani cloak and two Hibarah cloaks."
"10417","10388 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated, Abu Bakr al-Dahiri narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two seekers never sate: a seeker of knowledge and a seeker of the world."
"10418","10389 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uthman ibn Yahya al-Qirqisani narrated, Abd al-Majid narrated, from Marwan ibn Salim, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb and Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave the Turks while they leave you; the first to strip my community of its rule and what Allah entrusted them are the sons of Qantura."
"10419","10390 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Thabit ibn Ayyash al-Ahdab narrated, Abu Raja al-Kalbi narrated, al-Amash narrated, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Forty men of my community will remain, their hearts upon the heart of Ibrahim; Allah repels from the people of earth through them; they are called the Abdal. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They did not attain it by prayer, fasting, or charity. They said: O Messenger of Allah, by what did they attain it? He said: By generosity and counsel to the Muslims."
"10420","10391 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Bishr narrated, Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Greeting is a name of Allah's names placed on earth; spread it among you. When a man greets people and they return it, he has a degree's merit over them for reminding them; if they do not return it, one better and purer than them returns it."
"10421","10392 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-Araj narrated, Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Madaini narrated, Warqa narrated, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"10422","10393 - Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Layth Abu al-Sabbah al-Haddadi narrated, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Rumi narrated, Ubaydullah ibn Said, guide of al-Amash, narrated, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Fire was stoked and Paradise brought near; O people of the chambers, had you known what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."
"10423","10394 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, they said: Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated, Sahl ibn Uthman al-Bajali narrated, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: After you is a time of patience; the one holding fast in it has the reward of fifty martyrs. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, of us or of them? He said: Of you."
"10424","10395 - Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Munabbih ibn Uthman narrated, my father narrated, from Marwan ibn Salim, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a horse that grazed freely; it pleased him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This horse of mine is but a sea."
"10425","10396 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated, Ata ibn Muslim narrated, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will not enter Paradise until you believe, nor believe until you love one another. Shall I guide you to something which, if you do it, you will love one another? Spreading greeting among you."
"10426","10397 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hatim al-Askari narrated, Bishr ibn Mihran narrated, Sharik narrated, from Uthman ibn al-Mughirah, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Ibn Masud, he said: The first thing I knew of the Messenger of Allah's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) affair: I came to Mecca with uncles of mine, and we were directed to al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib. We came to him sitting by Zamzam and sat with him. While we were with him, a man came from the Safa gate, fair with redness, with flowing hair curled to his earlobes, high-nosed, aquiline, thin-nosed, bright of teeth, wide black-eyed, thick-bearded, thin of the line of hair on the chest, coarse of hands and feet, wearing two white garments, as the moon on the night of full moon. Walking on his right a beardless youth, handsome, adolescent or pubescent, followed by a woman who had veiled her charms, until he headed to the Stone and touched it, then the youth touched it, then the woman touched it. Then he circuited the House seven times, the youth and woman circuiting with him. Then he touched the corner, raised his hands and said the takbir; the youth stood on his right raising his hands, the woman stood behind them raising her hands and saying the takbir. He prolonged standing, bowed long, raised his head from bowing, stood supplicating, then prostrated, the youth and woman prostrating with him, doing as he did and following him. He said: We saw something unknown to us in Mecca and disapproved; we turned to al-Abbas and said: O Abu al-Fadl, this religion we did not know among you; has something happened? He said: Yes by Allah; do you not know this? We said: No. He said: This is my nephew Muhammad ibn Abdullah, the youth Ali ibn Abi Talib, and the woman Khadijah daughter of Khuwaylid. By Allah, none on earth's back worships Allah upon this religion but these three."
"10427","10398 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nizak al-Tusi narrated, Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, from al-Harith ibn Hasirah, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise are a hundred and twenty rows; my community is eighty rows of them."
"10428","10399 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Abu Shihab narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother beyond three."
"10429","10400 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated, Ali ibn Abis narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: Aishah had a freed slave of the children of Ismail; captives of Balu Anbar came, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded her to free some of them, and said: Whoever has a freed slave of the children of Ismail, let him free none of Himyar. Ali ibn Abis said: I said to Ismail ibn Abi Khalid: What was Himyar? He said: He is greater than Ismail."
"10430","10401 - Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Ayyub al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan al-Hadhdha narrated, al-Dahhak ibn Zayd al-Ahwazi informed us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, you are troubled. He said: Why should I not be troubled when the dirt of one of you is between his nail and fingertips?"
"10431","10402 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Faydi narrated, Jabir ibn Nuh narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I precede you at the Basin, and I shall vie in numbers with the nations through you; do not fight one another after me."
"10432","10403 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Basri narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated, Hushaym narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one's term is in a land, a need brings him to it."
"10433","10404 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abs al-Tanukhi narrated, Yahya ibn Yala narrated, from Isa ibn al-Musayyab, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abdullah, he said: We were commanded to fulfill oaths."
"10434","10405 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Harami ibn Hafs al-Qasmali narrated, Ziyad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Qurashi narrated, Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The upper hand is better than the lower hand; begin with those you support: your mother and father, your sister and brother, then nearest, nearest."
"10435","10406 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, they said: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated, Amr ibn Qays narrated, from Asim, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow Hajj with Umrah, for they remove poverty and sins as the bellows removes dross of iron, gold and silver; the accepted Hajj has no reward but Paradise."
"10436","10407 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, al-Fayd ibn Wathiq narrated, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated, Ikrimah ibn Abdullah al-Bunani narrated, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The slain will come holding his killer, his jugular veins gushing blood, before the Possessor of Might, saying: My Lord, ask this one for what he killed me. He says: For what did you kill him? If he says: I killed him that might belong to so-and-so, He says: It belongs to Allah."
"10437","10408 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated, Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim narrated, Asim narrated, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Emigrants, the Helpers, the freed of Quraysh, and the freed of Thaqif are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter."
"10438","10409 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Bukayr al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Ibn Aishah narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I precede you at the Basin."
"10439","10410 - Shuayb ibn Imran al-Askari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Askari narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, Abu Ayyub al-Afriqi narrated to me, from Asim, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies ascribing a rival to Allah, Allah places him in the Fire. Abdullah said: And another I did not hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I hope it is true: No servant dies not ascribing a rival to Allah but Allah admits him to Paradise."
"10440","10411 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, Abu Ayyub narrated to me, from Asim, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: The sunna in washing from major impurity is to wash your hands till clean, enter your right into the vessel and pour with your right upon your left, washing your private part till clean; then strike your left upon wall and ground and rub it, pour upon it with your right and wash it, then perform your ablution for prayer."
"10441","10412 - Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran al-Naqid narrated to us, Bashshar ibn Musa al-Khaffaf narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every act of kindness is charity."
"10442","10413 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated, Za'idah narrated, from Asim, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Among the worst of people are those whom the Hour overtakes while they are alive, and those who take graves as mosques."
"10443","10414 - Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Haytham al-Mu'adhdhin narrated, my father al-Haytham ibn al-Jahm narrated, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque in which there were women of the Ansar, so he exhorted them and reminded them and said: There is no woman among you whose three children die except that she will enter Paradise. A woman among them, not of the most prominent of them, said: O Messenger of Allah, and those with two? He said: And those with two."
"10444","10415 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated, Aban ibn Yazid narrated, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How bad it is for one of you to say: I forgot verse such-and-such; rather, he was made to forget. Keep to the Qur'an, for it is untamed, and it escapes from the hearts of men more than camels escape from their hobbles."
"10445","10416 - Abu Umar al-Darir Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Kufi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies setting up a rival to Allah will enter the Fire; and the obligatory prayers are expiations for what is between them so long as major sins are avoided."
"10446","10417 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ayyub Sahib al-Basri narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he raised it, he said: Prompt your dying ones with: There is no god but Allah; for the soul of the believer comes out with sweat, and the soul of the disbeliever comes out from his jaw, as the soul of a donkey comes out."
"10447","10418 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani al-Akhram narrated to us, Khallad ibn Aslam narrated, Hunayfah ibn Marzuq narrated, from Sharik, from Asim and al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Keep to the Qur'an, for it escapes from the hearts of men more than livestock escape from their hobbles."
"10448","10419 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated, Amr ibn Asim narrated, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated, from his father, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A woman should not touch another woman, for she then describes her to her husband, or to a man, as if he is looking at her. And when there are three, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of their companion, for that grieves him."
"10449","10420 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, al-Mas'udi narrated, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are three, and he mentioned the like of it, and he added in it: Whoever swears an oath in order to cut off thereby the property of a Muslim man will meet Allah while He is angry with him."
"10450","10421 - al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid al-Jarudi narrated, my father narrated, Sa'id ibn Zayd narrated, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us al-istikhara: O Allah, I seek good from You by Your knowledge, and I seek power from You by Your power, and I ask You of Your bounty; for You decree and I do not decree, and You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if this matter is good for me in my religion, and good for me in my livelihood, and good for me in what I seek good through, then choose it for me in well-being, make it easy for me, and bless me in it; and if other than that is better for me, then decree good for me wherever it is."
"10451","10422 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi narrated to me, Abu Tumaylah narrated, from al-Husayn ibn Waqid, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade the meat of domestic donkeys because they were working animals."
"10452","10423 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Ihab narrated, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I saw Gabriel, upon him be peace, having six hundred wings."
"10453","10424 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Walid al-Anbari narrated, Habban ibn Hilal narrated, Sadaqah al-Rummani narrated, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he raised it, he said: The most beloved of you to me on the Day of Resurrection are the best of you in character, and the most hateful of you to me on the Day of Resurrection are the chatterers and the pompous talkers. I said to Ibn Bahdalah: Who are the pompous talkers? He said: The arrogant."
"10454","10425 - al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Yasir al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn al-Azhar al-Wasiti narrated, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated, from Sharik, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The first thing judged among people is concerning blood, and the first thing the servant is taken to account for is prayer."
"10455","10426 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated, Sharik narrated, from Jami' ibn Abi Rashid, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us these words: O Allah, set right our relations, join our hearts, guide us to the paths of peace, save us from darkness into light, keep us away from shameful deeds, what is apparent of them and what is hidden. O Allah, bless us in our hearing, our sight, our hearts, our spouses and our offspring, turn to us in forgiveness; indeed You are the Oft-Returning, the Merciful; make us thankful for Your blessing, praising it and acknowledging it, and complete it upon us."
"10456","10427 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Jami' ibn Abi Rashid, from Abu Wa'il, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Mecca while around the House there were three hundred and sixty idols, so he began striking them with a stick in his hand, saying: Truth has come and falsehood has perished; indeed falsehood is ever perishing. Truth has come, and falsehood neither originates nor repeats."
"10457","10428 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, my father narrated, from al-Ala' ibn Khalid, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Hell will be brought, led by seventy thousand reins, with each rein seventy thousand angels dragging it."
"10458","10429 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated, Amr ibn Asim narrated, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated, he said: I heard my father, from al-A'mash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no soul killed unjustly except that a share of it is upon the son of Adam. Thus Sulayman al-Taymi narrated it, from al-A'mash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Shaqiq; and people said: from al-A'mash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq."
"10459","10430 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruq al-Kufi narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, he said: Abdullah said: I am informed of your place, and nothing prevents me from coming out to you except dislike of boring you; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to choose suitable times to exhort us, out of dislike of wearying us."
"10460","10431 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, from al-A'mash, he said: And Amr ibn Murrah narrated to me, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, the like of it."
"10461","10432 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hafs Umar ibn Yazid al-Raffa' al-Basri narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is the matter with people who honor the affluent and belittle the worshippers, and act upon the Qur'an in what agrees with their desires, and abandon what opposes their desires; then they believe in part and disbelieve in part; they strive for what is attained without striving, of the decreed decree, the written term, and the apportioned provision, and they do not strive for what is attained only by striving, of the ample recompense, the appreciated effort, and the trade that never perishes."
"10462","10433 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: A man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, how can I know when I have done good and when I have done bad? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hear your neighbors saying: You have done good, then you have done good; and when you hear them saying: You have done bad, then you have done bad."
"10463","10434 - Abu Shu'ayb Abdullah ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, my grandfather Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb narrated, al-Harith ibn Umayr narrated, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in a prayer, either adding in it or omitting; some of them said to him: Has something new happened in the prayer? He said: Nothing new has happened in it; had anything new happened I would have told you; but I am a human who forgets, so when I forget remind me. Then he prayed what remained of his prayer, then prostrated two prostrations of forgetfulness, then said: When one of you prays and does not know whether he added or omitted, let him seek what is correct, then prostrate two prostrations while sitting."
"10464","10435 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Maqabiri narrated, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated, Ayyub narrated, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir this hadith; then I met Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir and asked him about it, and he narrated to us from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that he said concerning recitation behind the imam: Be silent for the recitation as you were commanded, for prayer occupies; and the imam will suffice you that."
"10465","10436 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Abduh ibn Abi Lubabah narrated to me, that Shaqiq ibn Salamah said: I heard Ibn Mas'ud say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: How bad it is for a man - or a woman - to say: I forgot such-and-such sura, or such-and-such verse; rather, he was made to forget."
"10466","10437 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to me, Abd al-Warith narrated, Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated, from Abduh ibn Abi Lubabah, from Abu Wa'il, from Ibn Mas'ud, and he mentioned the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: None of you should say: I forgot verse such-and-such; for he did not forget, but he was made to forget."
"10467","10438 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, and Abdullah ibn Musa ibn Abi Uthman al-Anmati narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated, Mubarak ibn Fudalah informed us, from Ibrahim Abu Isma'il, Abu Wa'il Shaqiq ibn Salamah informed us, he said: I entered upon Ibn Mas'ud on the day of Ashura while he was eating fresh dates, and he said: This is the day of Ashura, a day we were commanded to fast before Ramadan was revealed."
"10468","10439 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: al-Hudhayl ibn Ibrahim al-Himmani narrated, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Qurashi narrated, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."
"10469","10440 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated, Sallam al-Tawil narrated, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The drop remains in the womb forty days, then it is likewise a clot, then it is likewise a lump; then Allah sends the angel with four words, and he writes his provision, his term, and whether wretched or happy. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of you does the deeds of the people of Paradise until there is only a cubit between him and Paradise, then the writing that preceded overtakes him, and he does the deeds of the people of the Fire until he dies; and one of you does the deeds of the people of the Fire until there is only a cubit between him and it, then the writing that preceded overtakes him, and he does the deeds of the people of Paradise before he dies."
"10470","10441 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Yazid al-Tahhan narrated, Sa'id ibn Khuthaym al-Hilali narrated, Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Dabbi narrated, from al-Hakam, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he raised it, he said: No one is more jealous than Allah; therefore He forbade shameful deeds, what is apparent of them and what is hidden."
"10471","10442 - Bakr ibn Muqbil al-Basri narrated to us, al-Khalil ibn Rashid al-Nushajani narrated, Ruwaym ibn Yazid al-Muqri' narrated, Sawwar ibn Mus'ab narrated, from Amr ibn Qays, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Shaqiq, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: A man came to Fatimah and said: O daughter of the Messenger of Allah, did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leave with you anything to present to me? She said: O slave girl, bring that palm stalk. She sought it and did not find it, so she said: Woe to you, seek it, for it equals Hasan and Husayn in my sight. She sought it and found it swept into her sweepings, and in it was: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of the believers whose neighbor is not safe from his harms. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent. Indeed Allah loves the modest, forbearing, chaste one who guards his chastity, and hates the obscene, foul-mouthed beggar who importunes. Modesty is of faith, and faith is in Paradise; obscenity is of foul speech, and foul speech is in the Fire."
"10472","10443 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il narrated, Mindal narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to his wife, let him cover himself, and let them not strip like two donkeys strip."
"10473","10444 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan narrated, Isra'il narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Answer the caller, do not refuse a gift, and do not beat people, or Muslims."
"10474","10445 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub Sahib al-Maghazi narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion."
"10475","10446 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Awn ibn Sallam narrated, Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, that he climbed al-Safa and seized his tongue and said: O tongue, speak good and you will gain, and be silent from evil and you will be safe, before you regret. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Most of the sins of the son of Adam are in his tongue."
"10476","10447 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr al-Asadi narrated, Talhah ibn Zayd narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever has a daughter and disciplines her well, teaches her well, and provides for her amply from the blessings Allah bestowed upon him, she will be for him a protection and a veil from the Fire."
"10477","10448 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated, Mushir ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Sal' al-Hamdani narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When my Companions are mentioned, refrain; when the stars are mentioned, refrain; and when destiny is mentioned, refrain."
"10478","10449 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated, Muhammad ibn Sawa' narrated, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep the Qur'an in memory, for it escapes from the hearts of men more than livestock escape from their hobbles; and how bad it is for one of you to say: I forgot verse such-and-such; rather, he was made to forget."
"10479","10450 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, al-Rabi' ibn Badr narrated, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Qur'an is an intercessor whose intercession is accepted, and an accuser whose word is believed. Whoever puts it before him, it leads him to Paradise; and whoever puts it behind him, it drives him to the Fire."
"10480","10451 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Duhaym narrated, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yusuf, from Sulayman ibn Mihran, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Of the approach of the Hour is the swelling of the crescents."
"10481","10452 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sudran narrated, Bazigh Abu al-Khalil al-Khassaf narrated, al-A'mash narrated, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be in the end of time a people who sit in mosques in circles, their leader is the world; so do not sit with them, for Allah has no need of them."
"10482","10453 - Abdan ibn Ahmad and Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, they said: Ammar ibn Umar ibn al-Mukhtar narrated, my father narrated to me, Ghalib al-Qattan narrated to me, he said: I came to Kufa on trade and lodged near al-A'mash. One night when I wanted to depart, he stood and prayed tahajjud at night, and passed by this verse: Allah bears witness that there is no god but He, and the angels and those of knowledge, maintaining justice; there is no god but He, the Mighty, the Wise. Indeed religion with Allah is Islam. Then al-A'mash said: And I bear witness to what Allah bore witness to, and I entrust this testimony to Allah, and it is with Allah a trust: Indeed religion with Allah is Islam. He said it repeatedly. I said: He must have heard something about it. I went to him in the morning and bade him farewell, then said: O Abu Muhammad, I heard you repeating this verse. He said: Has what is in it not reached you? I said: I have been with you for a month and you have not narrated to me. He said: By Allah, I shall narrate it to you in a year. So I stayed a year and remained at his door; when the year passed I said: O Abu Muhammad, the year has passed. He said: Abu Wa'il narrated to me, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Its companion will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic will say: My servant made a covenant with Me, and I am the most worthy to fulfill the covenant; admit My servant to Paradise."
"10483","10454 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Mahdi al-Missisi narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The straight path is that upon which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left us."
"10484","10455 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ishaq ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated, from Abu Ishaq al-Fazari, and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Musa al-Antaki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm narrated, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no days in which deeds are better than the ten days. It was said: Not even jihad in the cause of Allah? He said: Not even jihad in the cause of Allah."
"10485","10456 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated, Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: We were commanded to prostrate upon seven bones, and not to gather hair or garment."
"10486","10457 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafi'i narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I taken a close friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend."
"10487","10458 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafi'i narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: We used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and not perform ablution on account of treading."
"10488","10459 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ya'la ibn al-Minhal al-Sakuni narrated, Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The dead are punished in their graves, such that even beasts hear their voices."
"10489","10460 - al-Husayn ibn Ja'far al-Qattat al-Kufi and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Awn ibn Sallam narrated, Amr ibn Shamir narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he raised it, he said: A Muslim man does good with his third at his death, and Allah thereby completes his zakat."
"10490","10461 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated, al-Rabi' ibn Badr narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: People are two men: a scholar and a learner; and there is no good in other than them."
"10491","10462 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, Isma'il ibn Abdullah al-Kindi narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning His saying: He will pay them their rewards and increase them of His bounty: Their rewards: He admits them to Paradise; and He increases them of His bounty: intercession for those for whom intercession is due, for those who did good to them in the world."
"10492","10463 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Dinar narrated, Ubayd al-Nahhas narrated, from Amr ibn Shamir, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."
"10493","10464 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Mu'min al-Wasiti narrated, Awn ibn Umarah narrated, Bishr, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated, from Sulayman al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a rider came and made his camel kneel by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come to you from a nine-day journey; I have wearied my body, kept my night awake, and made my day thirsty, to ask you about two traits that have kept me awake. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What is your name? He said: I am Zayd al-Khayl. He said: Rather you are Zayd al-Khayr. He said: I ask you about the sign of Allah in one He wants, and His sign in one He does not want. I love good and its people and whoever acts upon it; if I act upon it I am certain of its reward, and if something of it escapes me I yearn for it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sign of Allah in one He wants, and His sign in one He does not want: had He wanted you for the other, He would have prepared you for it; then He would not care in which valley you walked."
"10494","10465 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Abdi narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariyya al-Kufi narrated, al-A'mash narrated, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah: So divorce them for their waiting period. Abdullah said: Divorce is in a period of purity without intercourse."
"10495","10466 - Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-Attar Abu Ayyub al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated, he said: I heard my father; al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed me, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq, that Ibn Mas'ud narrated to him, that the eighteen who were killed of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Badr, Allah placed their souls in Paradise in green birds roaming in Paradise. He said: While they were thus, your Lord looked upon them with a look and said: O My servants, what do you desire? They said: O our Lord, there is nothing beyond this. He said: And He says: My servants, what do you desire? And on the fourth they say: Return our souls to our bodies so we may be killed as we were killed."
"10496","10467 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah ibn Ma'n narrated, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq, he said: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said: There was a man who committed sins until he amassed wealth thereby. When death came to him he said to his family: If you follow what I command you, I shall give you my wealth; otherwise I shall not. They said: We shall follow what you command us. He said: When I die, burn me with fire, then crush my bones thoroughly; and when you see a day of strong wind, climb to a mountain top and scatter me in the wind. He said: And they did it. Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And he fell into the hand of Allah, and He said to him: What drove you to what you did? He said: Fear of You. He said: I have forgiven you."
"10497","10468 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated, Ubayd ibn al-Qasim narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: A Jew came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Excellent is your nation, were it not that they make equals. He said: How do they make equals? He said: They say: What Allah wills and you will. He said: He indeed says a word; say: What Allah wills, then you will. And he also said: Excellent is your nation, were it not that they associate. He said: What do they say? He said: They say: By the right of so-and-so, and by the life of so-and-so. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears, let him swear only by Allah."
"10498","10469 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Abdullah ibn Sufyan narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to go out to Bahrayn for trade. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray two units."
"10499","10470 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Faraj ibn Kurdi narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj al-Lakhmi narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had religion been suspended from the Pleiades, men of the sons of Persia would have reached it."
"10500","10471 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Hakkam narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Wasil, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, and he thinks he raised it, he said: Before the Hour there are days of killing, in which knowledge is lifted and ignorance descends."
"10501","10472 - Aslam ibn Sahl narrated to us, Umar ibn Salih ibn Jubayrah narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Atiyyah narrated, Muhammad ibn Suqah narrated, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to put his hands between his knees in prayer."
"10502","10473 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Umar ibn Salih ibn Jubayrah al-Wasiti narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Atiyyah narrated, Muhammad ibn Suqah narrated, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Ibn Mas'ud, that he sent to his brothers of the people of Kufa and ordered them to gather to bid them farewell. They gathered in the shade of the mosque, and he came to them, greeted them, and ordered them not to dispute over the Qur'an. He informed them that whoever denies anything of it has denied all of it. He informed them that they used to dispute over it with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they would recite to him and he would tell them all that they did well. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Tongues do not differ over it, nor does it wear out from much repetition; for the law of Islam in it is one: its limits and obligations. Had one of the two readings commanded something the other forbade, and obligations and limits differed in it - and he mentioned a word - and had I known one more knowledgeable than me in what was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), reachable by camel, I would have gone to him until I joined his knowledge to mine. I recited seventy suras from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the Qur'an was presented to him every year, and I would present to him and he would tell me I did well, until the year in which he died, when it was presented twice. Then I recited to him, and I shall not abandon it out of aversion to it."
"10503","10474 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Bukayr al-Hadrami narrated, Ja'far ibn Awn narrated, from al-Mu'alla ibn Irfan, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) apply kohl to the eye of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, with his saliva."
"10504","10475 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara' narrated to us, al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated, Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from al-Mu'alla ibn Irfan, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to breathe in the vessel three breaths, naming Allah at each breath, and giving thanks at the end of them."
"10505","10476 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my uncle al-Qasim narrated, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among people are keys to the remembrance of Allah; when they are seen, Allah is remembered."
"10506","10477 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Hurayth narrated, Abd al-Rahim ibn Zayd al-Ammi narrated, from his father, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning the saying of Allah the Mighty and Majestic: For Allah is his protector, and Gabriel, and the righteous of the believers. He said: The righteous of the believers are Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them."
"10507","10478 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Musabbih narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, Isma'il ibn Sumay' narrated, from Muslim al-Batin, from Abu Wa'il, he said: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said: This verse was revealed: Indeed those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price. Nothing abrogated it. Whatever man cuts off the property of a Muslim man by his oath is of the people of this verse."
"10508","10479 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated, Sharik narrated, from Uthman ibn Abi Zur'ah, from Abu Sadiq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise has eight gates; seven closed, and a gate open for repentance until the sun rises from its direction."
"10509","10480 - Abdullah ibn Najiyah narrated to us, Abu Burayd Amr ibn Yazid al-Jarmi narrated, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid: I saw Ibn Mas'ud stone the Jamrah, placing Mina on his right and Mecca on his left, and he stoned it with seven pebbles, then said: This is the station of the one upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was revealed."
"10510","10481 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Yahya ibn Adam narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Husayn, from Kathir ibn Mudrik, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, that he recited talbiyah on the night of Muzdalifah, then said: Here I saw the one upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was revealed reciting talbiyah."
"10511","10482 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Simak ibn Harb and al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I attained from her everything except intercourse - meaning from a woman - so Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and approaches of the night; indeed good deeds remove evil deeds."
"10512","10483 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from al-Hasan ibn Amr, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not a slanderer, nor a curser, nor obscene, nor foul-mouthed."
"10513","10484 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh al-Anbari narrated to me, my father narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Ali ibn Mudrik, from al-Rabi' ibn Khuthaym, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Is one of you unable to recite a third of the Qur'an in a night? They said: Who can bear that? He said: Rather, Say: He is Allah, the One."
"10514","10485 - Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Husayn, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from al-Rabi' ibn Khuthaym, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Say: He is Allah, the One equals a third of the Qur'an."
"10515","10486 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, they said: Abu Kurayb narrated, Yahya ibn Adam narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from al-A'mash, from Mansur, from Rib'i, from Abdullah, he raised it, he said: Three Allah loves: a man who rises at night reciting the Book of Allah, a man who gives charity hiding it from his left, and a man who was in a detachment whose companions fled, so he faced the enemy."
"10516","10487 - Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah narrated, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All flies are in the Fire except the bee."
"10517","10488 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashir al-Kindi narrated, al-Qasim ibn Malik narrated, from al-Ala' ibn al-Musayyab, from his father, or from Khaythamah, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: Moderation in a sunna is better than exertion in an innovation."
"10518","10489 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated, Bakr ibn Yazid al-Tawil narrated, Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah narrated, he said: I heard al-Musayyab ibn Rafi' narrate, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salams in the two prostrations of forgetfulness, to his right and to his left."
"10519","10490 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt al-Kufi and Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated, they said: Ali ibn Abis narrated, from al-Ala' ibn al-Musayyab, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless my nation in its early morning."
"10520","10491 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn al-Sammak narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not buy fish in water, for it is uncertainty. Abdullah said: My father said: And Hushaym narrated it to us and did not raise it."
"10521","10492 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Yasar al-Bajali narrated, Abu Kudaynah narrated, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a snake has seven good deeds, whoever kills a gecko has one good deed, and whoever leaves a snake for fear of pursuit is not of us."
"10522","10493 - al-Qasim ibn al-Dallal al-Kufi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Taghlibi narrated, Abdullah ibn Bukayr al-Ghanawi narrated, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Yahya ibn Hani', from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: We were forbidden from burrowing deep."
"10523","10494 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abu Sa'd al-Azdi, from Abu al-Kanud, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a gold ring or a gold circle."
"10524","10495 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jubarah ibn Mughallis narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu al-Kanud Abdullah ibn Uwaymir, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gold rings."
"10525","10496 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from al-Kalbi, al-Sha'bi narrated to me, from al-Harith, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that Abu Bakr went out, nothing brought him out but hunger; and Umar went out, nothing brought him out but hunger; and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to them, and they told him nothing brought them out but hunger. He said: Come with us to the house of a man of the Ansar called Abu al-Haytham ibn al-Tayyihan. He was not in the house; he had gone to fetch water. The woman welcomed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his two companions, spread something for them, and they sat upon it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked her: Where has Abu al-Haytham gone? She said: He has gone to fetch sweet water for us. He had not waited long before he came with a waterskin containing water, hung it, and wanted to slaughter a sheep for them; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seemed to dislike that for them. He said: So he slaughtered a young goat for them, then went and brought clusters of dates; they ate of that meat and unripe and ripe dates, and drank of the water. One of them, either Abu Bakr or Umar, said: This is of the bliss we shall be questioned about. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not reproached for anything he attains in the world; only the disbeliever is reproached."
"10526","10497 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan narrated, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi narrated, Abdullah ibn Bishr narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection are a man who killed a prophet or was killed by a prophet, a man who misleads people without knowledge, or an image-maker who makes statues."
"10527","10498 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Burjulani narrated, Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated, from Ja'far ibn al-Harith, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah, from his father, he said: I prayed with al-Walid ibn Uqbah and he shortened the takbir. Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said: They have shortened it, may Allah shorten them. By the One who sent Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the truth, I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten years and he did not shorten it once."
"10528","10499 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, they said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Imran al-Qattan informed us, from Qatadah, from Abd Rabbih, from Abu Iyad, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say in the sermon of need: Praise be to Allah, we seek His help and seek His forgiveness; we seek refuge in Allah from the evils of our souls. Whomever Allah guides, none misguides him; and whomever He misguides, none guides him. I bear witness there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has attained guidance; and whoever disobeys them harms only himself, and shall not harm Allah at all."
"10529","10500 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, Yusuf al-Qadi, Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi, and Ahmad ibn Isma'il al-Abdi al-Basri narrated to us, they said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Imran al-Qattan informed us, from Qatadah, from Abd Rabbih, from Abu Iyad, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Beware of belittled sins, for they gather upon a man until they destroy him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck for them a likeness like a man in a barren land; the people's food preparation came, and one man brought a stick, and another brought a stick, until they gathered a pile and kindled a fire and cooked what was in it."
"10530","10501 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ruzayq al-Rasibi narrated, al-Mughirah ibn Siqlab narrated, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated, from Wabarah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bathing on Friday is a sunna."
"10531","10502 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Hasan ibn Atiyyah narrated, from Qays ibn al-Rabi', from Imran ibn Zibyan, from Abu Tahya, Abdullah said: I heard from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad a virtue, that it be mine is dearer to me than what the sun rose upon. He stood to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Badr and said: We shall not say to you as the people of Moses said: Go, you and your Lord, the verse; but we shall fight on your right and your left. And I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), its lines relaxed with joy."
"10532","10503 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah narrated, my father narrated, from al-Nadr ibn Muhammad, from al-Ala' ibn al-Musayyab, from Fudayl ibn Amr, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, he said: Abdullah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Incantations, amulets, and love spells are polytheism."
"10533","10504 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Saminah narrated, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, from al-A'mash, Abu al-Sawwar narrated, Umayr ibn Sa'id narrated, he said: We were sitting with Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, and Abu Musa was with him. The governor seized a man, beat him, and mounted him upon a camel. People began saying: The camel, the camel. A man said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, is this the camel we used to hear of? He said: Then where is the lightning?"
"10534","10505 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Malih ibn Waki' narrated, my father narrated, from al-Mas'udi, from Bishr ibn Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah al-Bakka'i, from his father, he said: I was sitting with Abdullah and Hudhayfah, when a woman and a man passed by them upon a camel, their faces altered. One of them said to his companion: This is what we used to speak of. He said: No, with that is the lightning."
"10535","10506 - al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Subayh narrated, Isma'il ibn Aban narrated, Abd al-Malik ibn Uthman al-Thaqafi narrated, from Muhammad ibn Malik al-Hamdani, from his father Malik ibn Zubayd, from Abdullah, he said: A people came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with their companion and said: O Prophet of Allah, modesty has ruined our companion. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is of the laws of Islam, and foul speech is of the meanness of a man."
"10536","10507 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Asbahani al-Bazzaz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya Sa'iqah narrated, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated, Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Abbas narrated, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, he said: My father had stopped praying with us. I said: Why have you stopped praying with us? He said: You shorten. I said: And where is the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Among you are the old, the weak, and the needy? He said: I heard Abdullah ibn Mas'ud say that, then he prayed three times what you pray."
"10537","10508 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to me, my father narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Abu al-Safar, from al-Qa'qa', from Abdullah, he said: We were forbidden from the posteriors of women."
"10538","10509 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated, Salamah ibn Salih narrated, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Zahra', from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A people of Muslims who were punished in the Fire shall enter Paradise, by the mercy of Allah and the intercession of intercessors."
"10539","10510 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Shuja' narrated, al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated, from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not imagined falsely by whoever saw him."
"10540","10511 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, al-Mas'udi narrated, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Abdah al-Nahdi, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic has not forbidden a sanctity but that He knew one of you would violate it. I am holding your waistbands lest you plunge into the Fire as moths and flies plunge."
"10541","10512 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Khaba'iri narrated, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah, from Thumamah ibn Uqbah, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no man among a people who practice disobedience to Allah among them, they being more numerous and mightier than them, then they flatter him in his affair, except that Allah punishes them."
"10542","10513 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Kathir ibn Yahya Sahib al-Basri narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Intercession shall continue with people as they come out of the Fire, until even Iblis the chief of devils stretches forth hoping it reaches him."
"10543","10514 - Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Ayyub al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated, Sufyan al-Thawri, Sharik, and Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Sulayman al-A'mash, from Khaythamah, from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not please anyone at the displeasure of Allah, nor praise anyone for the bounty of Allah, nor blame anyone for what Allah has not given you; for the provision of Allah is not driven to you by the greed of the greedy, nor turned from you by the hatred of the hater. Allah in His apportioning and justice placed rest and joy in contentment and certainty, and placed worry and grief in displeasure."
"10544","10515 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Umar ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi narrated, Abu Nubatah Yunus ibn Yahya narrated, from Abbad ibn Kathir, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Khaythamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most severely punished of the people of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection are one who killed a prophet or was killed by a prophet, an unjust ruler, and these image-makers."
"10545","10516 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ja'far, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which wrong is greatest? He said: A cubit of land a believer deducts from the right of his brother; every pebble of either of them shall be hung around him on the Day of Resurrection."
"10546","10517 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Khalifah ibn Khayyat and Mahir ibn Nuh narrated, they said: al-Mufaddal ibn Ma'ruf narrated, Awn ibn Abi Rashid narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Rabb al-Ka'bah, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first of this nation are its best, and its last are its worst, differing and divided. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let death come to him while he treats people as he loves to be treated."
"10547","10518 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated, Ma'ruf ibn Hassan al-Samarqandi narrated, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the beast of one of you escapes in a barren land, let him call: O servants of Allah, hold it for me; O servants of Allah, hold it for me; for Allah has one present in the land who will hold it for you."
"10548","10519 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Sayrafi narrated, Sufyan ibn Mansur narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ziyad ibn Hudayr, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no night talk except for one praying or traveling."
"10549","10520 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Yahya ibn Adam narrated, from Yazid ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Kurdus, from Abdullah, he said: The chiefs of Quraysh passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while with him were people of the Muslims, and Suhayb and Khabbab. They said: O Muhammad, are these those upon whom Allah bestowed favor among us? Had you driven these away we would have followed you. So Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His face, up to His saying: Is not Allah most knowing of the grateful."
"10550","10521 - Ja'far ibn Ahmad al-Shami al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Mukhtar ibn Ghassan narrated, Yunus ibn Abi Ya'fur narrated, from his father, from Muslim, from Abu Sa'd, he said: I entered upon Ibn Mas'ud on the day of Ashura while he was eating. A man entered and Ibn Mas'ud said: Eat. He said: I am fasting. He said: Eat; this is a day fasted before Ramadan was revealed; then Ramadan came and this day was left."
"10551","10522 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja' narrated, Shayban informed us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is none of you but that a companion of his from the jinn has been assigned to him. It was said: And you? He said: And me; but Allah the Exalted aided me against him, so he submitted, and he commands me only with good."
"10552","10523 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from his father, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"10553","10524 - al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Mujashi'i al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Ya'qub al-Kirmani narrated, and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated, from his father, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"10554","10525 - Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hatim al-Tawil narrated, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Quddus narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan, from Zadha, he said: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined the first and Asr, and Maghrib and Isha. He was asked about it, and said: I did it so my nation would not be in hardship."
"10555","10526 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Amr ibn Makhlad narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariyya al-Ansari narrated, Harun ibn Antarah narrated, from Zadha, he said: I entered upon Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, while those wearing silk and brocade had preceded to his gathering. I said: You brought people near and kept me away. He said to me: Come near. He brought me near until he seated me upon his mat, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The two parents shall have a debt upon their child; on the Day of Resurrection they shall cling to him, and he shall say: I am your child; and they shall wish it were more than that."
"10556","10527 - Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated, from Sharik, from al-A'mash, from Abdullah ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadha, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Killing in the cause of Allah expiates all sins - or he said: everything - except trust. Trust is in prayer, trust is in fasting, trust is in speech; the severest of that is deposits. Sharik said: Ayyash al-Amiri narrated to me, from Zadha, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"10557","10528 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Farra' narrated, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abdullah ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadha, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic has angels traveling in the earth conveying to me greetings from my nation."
"10558","10529 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Barrah narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abdullah ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadha, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic has angels traveling in the earth conveying to me greetings from my nation."
"10559","10530 - Abu Umar al-Darir Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Umawi al-Kufi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abdullah ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadha, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has angels traveling in the earth conveying to me greetings from my nation."
"10560","10531 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated, and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated, they said: al-Saq' ibn Hazn narrated, Aqil al-Ja'di informed me, from Abu Ishaq al-Sabi'i, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me and said: O Ibn Mas'ud. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said it three times. Do you know which bond of faith is firmest? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The firmest bond of Islam is loyalty in it: love in it and hate. Then he said: O Ibn Mas'ud. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said it three times. He said: Do you know which people are best? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The best of people are the best of them in deeds when they understand their religion. Then he said: O Ibn Mas'ud. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Do you know which people are most knowledgeable? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The most knowledgeable of people are the most discerning of truth when people differ, even if short in deeds, even if crawling upon his buttocks. Those before me differed into seventy-two sects; three of them were saved and the rest perished: a group that supported the kings and fought them over their religion and the religion of Isa son of Maryam; they seized them, killed them, and cut them with saws. And a group that had no strength to oppose the kings, nor to dwell among them calling them to the religion of Allah the Mighty and Majestic and the religion of Isa son of Maryam, upon him be peace, so they wandered in the land and became monks. He said: And they are those of whom Allah the Mighty and Majestic said: And monasticism they invented, We did not prescribe it upon them, the verse. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believed in me, affirmed me, and followed me has observed it with its true observance; and whoever did not follow me, they are the perishing."
"10561","10532 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated, Zuhayr narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Abdullah al-Asamm, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A dream is glad tidings from Allah the Mighty and Majestic, and it is of seventy parts of prophethood. Your fire is of seventy parts of the poison of Hell. Whoever comes to the mosque awaiting prayer is in prayer so long as he does not break ablution; and whoever follows one prayer with another is in prayer so long as he does not break ablution."
"10562","10533 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Harami ibn Hafs al-Qasmali narrated, and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated, they said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Qasmali narrated, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Yahya ibn Ja'dah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None shall enter the Fire who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of faith; and none shall enter Paradise who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of pride. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, it pleases me that my garment be washed, my head oiled, and the strap of my sandal new; and he mentioned things until he mentioned the thong of the whip. Is that of pride, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, that is beauty; Allah the Mighty and Majestic is Beautiful and loves beauty; but pride is to despise truth and disdain people."
"10563","10534 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sallam al-Jumahi narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Yahya ibn Ja'dah ibn Hubayrah, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina he allotted houses, and allotted to Ibn Mas'ud among those he allotted. His companions said to him: O Messenger of Allah, move him away from us. He said: Then for what did Allah send me? Allah the Mighty and Majestic does not sanctify a nation that does not give the weak among them his right."
"10564","10535 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Barrah al-San'ani narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar, from Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Mecca on the day of conquest, while around the Ka'bah were three hundred and sixty idols; he began striking them, saying: Truth has come and falsehood has perished; indeed falsehood is ever perishing."
"10565","10536 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Isa ibn Dinar al-Mu'adhdhin, freedman of Amr ibn al-Harith al-Khuza'i, narrated, my father narrated to me, from Amr ibn al-Harith, that he heard Abdullah ibn Mas'ud say: I fasted with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) twenty-nine more often than I fasted with him thirty."
"10566","10537 - Ali ibn Ibrahim al-Amiri al-Kufi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated, from Abu Sa'd al-Baqqal, from Abdullah ibn Ma'qil, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever commits a mistake and a sin, then regrets, it is its expiation."
"10567","10538 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Sharik narrated, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi', from his father, from Abdullah, he raised it, he said: Riba, however much, its end becomes littleness."
"10568","10539 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated, from Isra'il, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi', from his father, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing much of riba except that its end is to littleness."
"10569","10540 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah narrated, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated, from Mis'ar ibn Kidam, from al-Rukayn, from his father, from Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A true righteous dream is a part of seventy-six parts of prophethood."
"10570","10541 - Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Hammad al-Barbari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated, al-Rabi' ibn Sahl narrated, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi', from his father, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It suffices a man who sees an evil he cannot change but that Allah knows he dislikes it."
"10571","10542 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, they said: Shadh ibn al-Fayyad narrated, Umar ibn Ibrahim narrated, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan, from Najiyah ibn Ka'b, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant is born a believer, lives a believer, and dies a disbeliever; and a servant is born a disbeliever, lives a disbeliever, and dies a believer. A servant acts a period of his life with happiness, then what was written for him overtakes him, and he dies wretched. And a servant acts a period of his life with wretchedness, then what was written for him overtakes him, and he dies happy."
"10572","10543 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Shadh ibn al-Fayyad narrated, Abu Hilal narrated, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan, from Najiyah ibn Ka'b, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah created Yahya son of Zakariyya in his mother's belly a believer, and created Pharaoh in his mother's belly a disbeliever."
"10573","10544 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Tahir ibn Abi Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, Yazid ibn Abdullah narrated to me, he said: I heard Amr ibn Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no two Muslims but that between them is a veil of Allah. If one of them says obscenity to his companion, he tears his veil. And if he says: O disbeliever, then one of them has disbelieved."
"10574","10545 - Abu Umar al-Darir Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Zuhayr narrated, from Mutarrif, from Abu al-Jahm, from al-Radrad, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: I used to greet the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he would return it to me. Then I greeted him and he did not return it to me. I said: I used to greet you and you would return it to me, then I greeted and you did not return it to me. He said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic brings about of His affair what He wills."
"10575","10546 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Khalid ibn Rib'i, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your companion is the close friend of Allah, meaning himself (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10576","10547 - Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated, Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated, from al-Walid ibn Qays, from Ishaq ibn Abi al-Kahtalah - Muhammad said: I think it is from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he saw Gabriel in his form only twice. As for once, he asked him to show himself in his form, and he showed him, coming filling the horizon. As for the second, he was with him when he ascended, in His saying: Then he drew near and descended, and was at two bows' length or nearer, and revealed to His servant what He revealed. When Gabriel perceived his Lord the Mighty and Majestic, he returned to his form. That is His saying: And he saw him another descent, at the Lote Tree of the Utmost, near it is the Garden of Refuge, up to His saying: He saw of the great signs of his Lord. He said: The creation of Gabriel."
"10577","10548 - al-Hasan ibn al-Sahl al-Mujawwiz al-Basri narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Habib al-Qanawi narrated, al-Mas'udi narrated, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Alqamah al-Thaqafi, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: We returned from the campaign of Hudaybiyah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will guard us tonight? Abdullah said: And I said: I, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will sleep. Then he repeated: Who will guard us tonight? And I said: I, until he repeated several times, three: I, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then you. So I guarded them until near dawn the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) overtook me: You will sleep. And I slept, and nothing woke us but the heat of the sun upon our backs. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and did as he used to do of ablution and the two units of Fajr, then led us in Subh. When he finished he said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic, had He wanted you not to sleep past it, you would not have slept; but He wanted it to be - or he said: to be - for those after you; thus for whoever sleeps or forgets. Then the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the camels of the people scattered. People went out seeking them, and brought their camels except the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Take here. I took where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told me, and found its halter twisted upon a tree; by Allah, none but a hand could have untied it. He said: And I brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: O Messenger of Allah, by the One who sent you with the truth, I found its halter twisted upon a tree, none but a hand could have untied it. He said: And there was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Indeed We granted you a clear victory."
"10578","10549 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated, Sufyan and Shu'bah narrated, they said: Jami' ibn Shaddad narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Alqamah, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Mas'ud say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram from Hudaybiyah. We traveled by night and camped on soft ground. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will guard us? Bilal said: I. He said: Then you will sleep. They slept until the sun rose. So-and-so and so-and-so awoke, among them Umar, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not awake. He said: Go down. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) awoke and said: Do as you used to do. When they did, he said: Thus for whoever of you sleeps or forgets."
"10579","10550 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Yahya ibn Adam narrated, from Hasan ibn Thabit, from Abdullah ibn al-Walid, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Alqamah al-Thaqafi, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: With us on the night the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept past Fajr until the sun rose were two guides."
"10580","10551 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated, my father narrated to me, Ibn Abi Layla narrated, from al-Hakam, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he said: Allah hears him who praises Him, he said: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise, filling the heavens, filling what is between them, and filling what You will of a thing thereafter; Possessor of praise, Possessor of grandeur and glory; none withholds what You give, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him nothing against You."
"10581","10552 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated, my father narrated to me, Ibn Abi Layla narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Babah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"10582","10553 - Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab al-Kufi narrated, Hibban ibn Ali narrated, from Husayn ibn Madh'ur, from Quraysh al-Tamimi, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no faith for one who has no trust, and no religion for one who has no covenant. By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the religion of a servant is not straight until his tongue is straight, and his tongue is not straight until his heart is straight. None shall enter Paradise whose neighbor is not safe from his harms. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what are harms? He said: His oppression and wrongdoing. Whatever man gains wealth from unlawful means and spends of it, it is not blessed for him; if he gives charity it is not accepted from him; and what remains is his provision to the Fire. The impure does not expiate the impure, but the pure expiates the impure."
"10583","10554 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated, Azrah Abu Asim narrated, he said: Umm al-Fayd, freedwoman of Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, narrated to me, she said: I heard Ibn Mas'ud say: Whoever supplicates with this supplication on the evening of Arafah, so long as he does not supplicate with sin or severing kinship, shall be answered: Glory to the One Whose throne is in heaven; glory to the One Whose foothold is in the earth; glory to the One Whose path is in the sea; glory to the One Whose decree is in graves; glory to the One Whose mercy is in Paradise; glory to the One Whose authority is in the Fire; glory to the One Whose spirit is in the air; glory to the One Who raised heaven; glory to the One Who laid earth; glory to the One from Whom there is no refuge but to Him. I said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said, as if annoyed: Yes."
"10584","10555 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Yazid ibn Qutaybah al-Harashi narrated, al-Fadl al-Agharr al-Kilabi narrated, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by his companions one day and said to them: Do you know what your Lord the Mighty and Majestic says? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said it three times. He said: By My might and majesty, no servant prays it at its time but I shall admit him to Paradise; and whoever prays it outside its time, if I will I shall mercy him, and if I will I shall punish him."
"10585","10556 - Abu Ubaydah Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim al-Askari narrated to us, Sayf ibn Miskin al-Uswari narrated, Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated, from al-Hasan, from Utayy al-Sa'di: Utayy said: I went out seeking knowledge until I came to Kufa, and Abdullah ibn Mas'ud was among the people of Kufa. I asked about him and was guided to him, and he was in the Grand Mosque. I came to him and said: Abu Abd al-Rahman, I have come traveling to you to learn from you, that Allah may benefit us through it after you. He said to me: Of which people is the man? I said: A man of Basra. He said: Of whom? I said: Of this tribe, of Banu Sa'd. He said to me: O Sa'di, I shall narrate among you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not guide you to a people abundant in wealth, strong in might, from whom you may gain abundant wealth, or he said: much. He said: Who are they? He said: They are this tribe, of Banu Sa'd of the sands. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Banu Sa'd with Allah are of great fortune. Ask, O Sa'di. I said: Abu Abd al-Rahman, has the Hour a knowledge by which the Hour is known? He was reclining and sat upright, and said: O Sa'di, you asked me of what I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about. I said: O Messenger of Allah, has the Hour a knowledge by which the Hour is known? He said to me: O Ibn Mas'ud, the Hour has signs, and the Hour has portents. Of the signs and portents of the Hour: children are anger, rain is heat, and evil ones overflow. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs and portents of the Hour: the liar is believed, and the truthful is disbelieved. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs and portents of the Hour: the treacherous is trusted, and the trustworthy is deemed treacherous. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs and portents of the Hour: dishes are joined, and kinship is cut. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs and portents of the Hour: hypocrites lead every tribe, and wicked men lead every market. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs and portents of the Hour: mosques are adorned, and hearts are ruined. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs and portents of the Hour: the believer in the tribe is humbler than a small sheep. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs and portents of the Hour: men suffice with men and women with women. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs and portents of the Hour: mosques are many and pulpits are high. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs and portents of the Hour: the ruin of the world is built, and its building is ruined. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs and portents of the Hour: musical instruments appear, and wines are drunk. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs and portents of the Hour: drinking wines. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs and portents of the Hour: policemen, slanderers, and fault-finders. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs and portents of the Hour: children of fornication are many. I said: Abu Abd al-Rahman, and are they Muslims? He said: Yes. I said: Abu Abd al-Rahman, and the Qur'an is among them? He said: Yes. I said: Abu Abd al-Rahman, and how is that? He said: There shall come upon people a time when a man divorces the woman, then denies his divorce and remains upon her private part; so they are two adulterers so long as they remain."
"10586","10557 - Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Thabit, from Safwan ibn Muhriz, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, or another, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Souls are assembled troops; those of them that recognized one another came together in harmony, and those of them that were strangers to one another differed."
"10587","10558 - Sulayman ibn al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, my father narrated, al-Qasim ibn Ma'in narrated, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not the adhan of Bilal prevent any of you from sahur; for he calls the adhan only so that your sleeper may wake, and your standing one may return, and dawn comes like this."
"10588","10559 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ali ibn Maymun al-Raqqi narrated, Ata ibn Muslim narrated, from Isma'il al-Kufi, from Asim, from Abu Uthman, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever drags his garments in arrogance, Allah will not look at him, neither in lawful nor in unlawful. This Isma'il is Ibn Abi Khalid, and Allah knows best."
"10589","10560 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Sallam ibn Abi Muti' narrated, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that a man kissed a woman, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I did such and such. Then Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the early hours of the night; indeed good deeds remove evil deeds. The man said: Is it for me, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, rather it is for my ummah."
"10590","10561 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Musa al-Ansari narrated, Asim ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ashja'i narrated, Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Qunfudh al-Taymi narrated, from Jabir ibn Silan, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about a man who performs ghusl from janabah but water misses part of his body. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He should wash that spot, then pray."
"10591","10562 - Muhammad ibn Zurayq ibn Jami' al-Misri narrated to us, Isa ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Amr ibn Abdullah al-Awdi, from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Shall I not inform you of who is forbidden to the Fire? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Every gentle, soft, approachable, easy one."
"10592","10563 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated, Yahya ibn Kathir narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Abu Ja'far al-Farra, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is invited to food, let him accept; if he is not fasting, let him eat, and if he is fasting, let him supplicate for blessing."
"10593","10564 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd al-Umari, from Umar ibn Abdullah, freedman of Ghufrah, from Abu al-Aswad al-Du'ali, he said: I disputed with the Qadariyyah and they cornered me, so I came to Imran ibn al-Husayn al-Khuza'i, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: O Abu Nujayd, I disputed with the Qadariyyah and they cornered me, so is there a hadith you can narrate to me that Allah may benefit me through? He said: Perhaps if I narrated a hadith to you, you would cover your ears over it as if you had not heard it. I said: I came only for that. He said: If Allah punished the inhabitants of heaven and the inhabitants of earth, He would punish them while He is not unjust to them; and if He admitted them into His mercy, His mercy would be vaster for them than their sins. It is as Allah the Mighty and Majestic said: He punishes whom He wills and forgives whom He wills. Whoever is punished, it is justice, and whoever is shown mercy, it is justice. If the mountains were gold or silver for one of you and he spent them in the path of Allah, then did not believe in qadar, its good and its evil, he would not benefit from that. Then I came to Abdullah ibn Mas'ud and asked him, and Abdullah said to Ubayy ibn Ka'b: O Abu al-Mundhir, narrate to him. Ubayy said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, narrate to him. So Ibn Mas'ud narrated the like of the hadith of Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and upon his family, abundant, good and blessed salutations."
"10594","773 - Hadiths of Abdullah ibn al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim ibn Abd Manaf, his kunyah Abu al-Abbas, and some of his reports and his death, may Allah be pleased with them both. 10565 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated, Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated, from Dawud ibn Ali, he said: Umm al-Fadl conceived in the Shi'b, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I hope that she will brighten our faces with a boy. Then she gave birth to Abdullah ibn Abbas."
"10595","10566 - Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Qurashi narrated, Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated, Ibn Abi Najih informed me, from Mujahid, he said: Ibn Abbas said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his household were in the Shi'b, my father came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, I see Umm al-Fadl as though she is carrying a pregnancy. He said: Perhaps Allah will gladden our eyes through her with a boy. Then I was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was in my swaddling cloth, and he performed tahnik for me. Mujahid said: We know of no one who received tahnik with the saliva of prophethood except him."
"10596","10567 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, he said: Abdullah ibn Abbas died at al-Ta'if in the year sixty-eight, at the age of seventy-two years, and he used to dye his beard yellow. He said: I was born three years before the Hijrah, while we were in the Shi'b; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died when I was thirteen years old."
"10597","10568 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini Fustuqah narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated, he said: Abdullah ibn Abbas died in the year sixty-eight."
"10598","10569 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini narrated to us, Abu Zayd Umar ibn Shabbah narrated, he said: I heard Abu Nu'aym say: Ibn Abbas died in the year sixty-eight."
"10599","10570 - Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham narrated, Ziyad ibn Abdullah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Ibn Abbas was tall, with a yellowish tinge in his complexion, bulky, handsome, bright-faced, with two braids."
"10600","10571 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, he said: I saw Ibn Abbas, and he had a jummah (hair reaching the shoulders)."
"10601","10572 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Zahmawayh narrated, Sharik narrated, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I saw Ibn Abbas during the days of Mina with long hair, wearing a waist-wrapper with some isbal in it, and a yellow upper garment."
"10602","10573 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Imran ibn Abi Ata, he said: I witnessed Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah when Ibn Abbas died at al-Ta'if; he said takbir over him four times, received him from the direction of the qiblah when he placed him in the grave, and pitched a tent over him for three days."
"10603","10574 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated, Hushaym narrated, Abu Hamzah Imran ibn Abi Ata narrated, he said: I witnessed the death of Ibn Abbas at al-Ta'if; Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah took charge of him, said takbir over him four times, placed him into the grave from the side of his feet, and pitched a tent over him."
"10604","10575 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated, Hushaym narrated, from Abu Ishaq al-Kufi, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken in death when I was ten years old."
"10605","10576 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from al-A'mash, from Ziyad ibn Husayn, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I recited al-Muhkam - meaning al-Mufassal - in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he was then twelve years old."
"10606","10577 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shu'bah informed, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died and I had recited al-Muhkam of the Qur'an. Shu'bah said: I said to Abu Bishr: What is al-Muhkam? He said: Al-Mufassal."
"10607","10578 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna ibn Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh al-Anbari narrated to us, my father narrated, my father narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died when I was fifteen years old, and I had been circumcised."
"10608","10579 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken in death when I was newly circumcised."
"10609","10580 - Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Hannat al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Rashad ibn Khuthaym al-Hilali narrated, my uncle Sa'id ibn Khuthaym al-Hilali narrated, Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan narrated, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith narrated to me, she said: While I was passing and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the Hijr, he said: O Umm al-Fadl. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You are pregnant with a boy. She said: How, when Quraysh have conspired that our women will not give birth? He said: It is as I tell you; when you deliver him, bring him to me. When she delivered him, she brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he named him Abdullah, fed him saliva from his own saliva, then said: Go with him, you will find him intelligent. She said: I came to al-Abbas and informed him; he dressed and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was a handsome man of tall stature. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him, he stood to him, kissed him between his eyes, sat him at his right, then said: This is my uncle; whoever wishes, let him boast of his uncle. Al-Abbas said: Some of this speech, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Why should I not say it, when you are my uncle and the remainder of my forefathers, and the uncle is a father."
"10610","10581 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Marwan ibn Shuja' narrated, Salim ibn Ajlan al-Jazari al-Aftas narrated, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: Ibn Abbas died at al-Ta'if, and I witnessed his funeral; a white bird, the like of whose beauty had not been seen, came until it entered his bier, then was not seen coming out of it. When he was buried, this verse was recited at the edge of the grave - we did not know who recited it: O tranquil soul, return to your Lord, well-pleased and pleasing, so enter among My servants, and enter My Paradise."
"10611","10582 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Marwan al-Kufi narrated, Umayy al-Sayrafi narrated, Abdullah ibn Yamin narrated from his father, he said: I witnessed the funeral of Ibn Abbas, and he died at al-Ta'if; when he was brought to the grave-pit, a white bird called al-ghurnuq came until it entered the inside of the bier and was not seen."
"10612","10583 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Bassam al-Sayrafi narrated, from Abdullah ibn Yamin, my father informed me that when the funeral of Ibn Abbas passed at al-Hirah - which is a valley of theirs - a white bird called al-ghurnuq came and entered the bier and was not seen afterwards."
"10613","And among the virtues of Abdullah ibn Abbas and his reports. 10584 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, Ammar ibn Abi Ammar informed, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I was with my father at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a man conversing privately with him, and he was as one turning away from my father. We left him, and my father said: Did you not see your cousin as one turning away from me? I said: Father, there was a man conversing privately with him. He said: Was there anyone with him? I said: Yes. We returned, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, I said to Abdullah such and such, and he said to me such and such; was there anyone with you? He said: Yes; did you see him, O Abdullah? I said: Yes. He said: That was Jibril, peace be upon him; he is the one who kept me from you."
"10614","10585 - Abdullah ibn Sa'd ibn Yahya al-Raqqi narrated to us, Amir ibn Sayyar narrated, Furat ibn al-Sa'ib narrated, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Abdullah ibn al-Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand on the head of Abdullah ibn al-Abbas and said: O Allah, grant him wisdom and teach him interpretation. And he placed his hand on his chest, and Abdullah ibn al-Abbas felt its coolness in his back, then said: O Allah, fill his inside with wisdom and knowledge. Then he never felt shy within himself about asking anyone among people, and he remained the scholar of this ummah until Allah took him."
"10615","10586 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Minhal ibn Bahr Abu Salamah al-Uqayli narrated, al-Ala ibn Burd narrated, al-Fadl ibn Habib narrated, from Furat, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I wore white clothes, and he was conversing privately with Dihyah ibn Khalifah al-Kalbi - and he was Jibril, peace be upon him, though I did not know - and I did not greet. Jibril said: O Muhammad, who is this? He said: This is my cousin, this is Ibn Abbas. He said: How intense is the whiteness of his clothes; his offspring shall rule after him. Had he greeted us we would have returned it to him. When I returned, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Ibn Abbas, what prevented you from greeting? I said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, I saw you conversing with Dihyah ibn Khalifah, so I disliked interrupting your private conversation. He said: And you saw him? I said: Yes. He said: Your sight shall go, and it shall be returned to you at your death. Ikrimah said: When Ibn Abbas died and was placed on his bier, a bird of intense brightness came and entered his shrouds; they wanted to unfold his shrouds, but Ikrimah said: What are you doing? This is the glad tidings of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which he told him. When he was placed in his lahd, he was met with a word heard by those at the edge of his grave: O tranquil soul, return to your Lord, well-pleased and pleasing, so enter among My servants, and enter My Paradise."
"10616","10587 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym informed, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I was in the house of Maymunah bint al-Harith, and I placed wudu water for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who placed this? Maymunah said: Abdullah placed it. He said: O Allah, teach him interpretation and give him understanding in religion."
"10617","10588 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, my father Ali ibn Asim narrated to me, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew me to himself and said: O Allah, teach him wisdom."
"10618","10589 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hashim ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Khuthaym al-Hilali narrated, Abu Amir al-Asadi narrated, Musa ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated, from his father, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, he said: Abdullah ibn Abbas sought permission to enter upon Mu'awiyah, while clans of Quraysh were gathered with him and Sa'id ibn al-As sat at his right. When Mu'awiyah saw him he said: O Sa'id, by Allah I shall put to Ibn Abbas questions he will fail to answer. Sa'id said to him: The like of Ibn Abbas will not fail your questions. When he sat, Mu'awiyah said to him: What do you say about Abu Bakr? He said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Bakr; by Allah he was a reciter of the Qur'an, distant from deviation, heedless of indecency, forbidding evil, knowledgeable in his religion, fearful of Allah, shunning ruinous things, standing in prayer at night, fasting by day, safe from his world, resolved upon justice to creation, commanding good, patient in it, thankful in all states, remembering Allah morning and evening, subduing his soul to good, surpassing his companions in piety and restraint, asceticism and chastity, righteousness and care, detachment and sufficiency; so Allah gave those who revile him curses until the Day of Resurrection. Mu'awiyah said: What do you say about Umar ibn al-Khattab? He said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Hafs; by Allah he was the ally of Islam, shelter of orphans, abode of faith, refuge of the weak, fortress of the upright, a stronghold for creation and a help for people; he stood for Allah's right patiently and seeking reward until Allah manifested the religion through him, conquered lands, and Allah was mentioned in regions and watering places, on hills, in outskirts and lands, dignified in obscenity, thankful in ease and hardship, ever remembering Allah, so Allah gave whoever belittles him the curse until the Day of Regret. Mu'awiyah said: What do you say about Uthman ibn Affan? He said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Amr; by Allah he was the noblest of grandchildren, best of the righteous, most patient of reciters, praying tahajjud in the late night, weeping much at Allah's remembrance, ever reflecting day and night on what concerns him, hastening to every noble deed, striving for every salvation, fleeing every ruin, the companion of the army and the well, and son-in-law of the Chosen one upon his two daughters; so Allah gave whoever reviles him remorse until the Day of Resurrection. Mu'awiyah said: What do you say about Ali ibn Abi Talib? He said: May Allah have mercy on Abu al-Hasan; by Allah he was the banner of guidance, cave of piety, abode of intellect, mountain of wisdom, light of night travel in the darkness, caller to the greatest proof, knower of what is in the former scriptures, upholder of interpretation and remembrance, attached to the means of guidance, abandoning injustice and harm, turning from paths of ruin, best of those who believed and feared, master of those who wore shirt and cloak, best of those who performed hajj and sa'i, most generous of those who judged justly, most eloquent of people except the prophets and the Chosen Prophet, companion of the two qiblahs - can any monotheist equal him - husband of the best of women and father of the two grandsons; my eye has not seen his like nor shall see until Resurrection and the Meeting; whoever curses him, upon him is Allah's curse and that of servants until the Day of Resurrection. He said: What do you say about Talhah and al-Zubayr? He said: Mercy of Allah upon them; by Allah they were chaste, Muslims, dutiful, pure, purified, martyrs, learned; they slipped a slip, and Allah will forgive them, Allah willing, by their early support, early companionship and beautiful deeds. Mu'awiyah said: What do you say about al-Abbas? He said: May Allah have mercy on Abu al-Fadl; by Allah he was the twin of the Messenger of Allah, delight of Allah's chosen, most munificent of peoples and chief of uncles, with insight in affairs and foresight of outcomes adorned by knowledge; lineages fade at mention of his virtue and genealogies recede at the pride of his clan; why should he not be so when reared by the noblest who moved and breathed, Abd al-Muttalib, proudest of near and rider? Mu'awiyah said: Why was Quraysh named Quraysh? He said: After a creature in the sea, the greatest of sea creatures in danger, which seizes nothing of sea creatures but eats it; so Quraysh was named because it is greatest of Arabs in deeds. He said: Do you narrate anything about that? He recited to him the verse of al-Jumahi. Mu'awiyah said: You spoke truth, O Ibn Abbas; I bear witness you are the tongue of your household. When Ibn Abbas left him, he said to those with him: I never spoke to him but found him prepared."
"10619","10590 - Ahmad ibn Hamdan ibn Musa al-Khallal al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb al-Junday Saburi narrated, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Dahah narrated, Abu Khidash Abd al-Rahman ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Amr ibn al-Ahtam al-Tamimi narrated, Aban ibn al-Walid narrated, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr wrote to Ibn Abbas about allegiance, and he refused to pledge to him. Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah thought he refused him only because of his standing, so Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah wrote to Ibn Abbas: To proceed, it has reached me that the deviant Ibn al-Zubayr invited you to his pledge to bring you into his obedience, that you be a helper upon falsehood and partner in sin, but you refused him and withdrew, for what Allah made you know of yourself regarding our right, O Household; may Allah reward you best as He rewards those who join kin and fulfill covenants. Whatever I forget, I shall not forget your kindness and joining, and your good reward, with what you deserve from us in obedience, honor and kinship to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Look to those of your people with you and those who come to you from distant lands whom Ibn al-Zubayr bewitches with his tongue and adorned speech; dissuade them from him, for they are more obedient to you and hear you more than they hear the deviant, ruined renegade. Peace. Ibn Abbas wrote to him: To proceed, your letter came to me mentioning Ibn al-Zubayr's invitation and that I refused out of knowledge of your right. If that is so, I do not seek your kindness thereby, but Allah knows what I intend. You wrote asking me to urge people to you and dissuade them from Ibn al-Zubayr - no joy nor delight; dust in your mouth; you are far off if your soul deludes you; you are the deprived, destroyed one. You wrote mentioning hastening my kindness and joining - withhold, O man, your kindness and joining from me, for I withhold from you my love and support. By my life, you give us of what is in your hands only little, and withhold much and long. May you have no father, do you think I forget your killing Husayn and the youths of Banu Abd al-Muttalib, lamps of darkness and stars of banners, whom your troops left by your order fallen in one ground, wrapped in blood, stripped in the open, neither shrouded nor pillowed, winds blowing over them, wolves attacking them, lame hyenas visiting them, until Allah provided for them people who did not share in their blood, who shrouded and buried them. By them, by Allah, and by me, Allah favored you so you sat in your seat wherein you are. Whatever I forget, I shall not forget your empowering over them the bastard son of a bastard, of the adulteress, distant in kin, base in father and mother; and what your father earned by claiming him - shame, sin, abasement and disgrace in this world and the next; for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. Your father claimed the child is not of the bed, and the adulterer is unharmed, and his child joins him as the child of a prostitute joins a guide. Your father killed the Sunnah in ignorance and revived misleading innovations deliberately. Whatever I forget, I shall not forget your driving Husayn from the sanctuary of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Allah's sanctuary, and your sending men to them and planting spies - if he senses you, hasten against him - until you forced him from Mecca to the land of Kufa, your horses and troops roaring at him like lions, enmity of your like to Allah, His Messenger and his Household. Then you wrote to Ibn Marjanah to meet him with horses, men, spears and swords, then wrote to him to hasten and not delay, until he killed him and those with him of the youths of Banu Abd al-Muttalib, the Household whom Allah removed impurity from and purified; we are they, not like your rude, harsh fathers, donkey livers. You knew he was noblest of the people of the valley in the valley of old, and noblest in it anew. They stayed in the two sanctuaries and deemed fighting lawful in them, but he disliked to be the one by whom Allah's sanctuary, His Messenger's sanctuary and the Sacred House are violated. Husayn sought truce from you and asked to return, but you seized upon his few helpers and the uprooting of his household, as if killing a household of Turks or Kabul. How do you find me upon your love and seek my support, when you killed my father's sons, your sword dripping with my blood, while you seek my vengeance? If Allah wills, my blood shall not remain long with you, nor outrun me in my vengeance; and if it outruns us, we accept what prophets and families of prophets accepted - their blood remained in this world, and the appointment is Allah; Allah suffices the wronged as helper and avenger of wrongdoers. Wonder of all wonders, as long as you live by your Lord. The wonder: your carrying the daughters of Abd al-Muttalib and their small young sons to you in Syria, showing people you conquered us and humiliate us; yet by them, by Allah, and by me, Allah favored you and your father and mother among women. By Allah, you spend morning and evening safe from my hand's wound, but your wound by my tongue, my undoing and binding, shall be greater; let not disputation provoke you, for Allah shall not grant you respite after your killing the progeny of His Messenger but a little, until He seizes you painfully and expels you from the world sinful, blameworthy. Live - may you have no father - as you wish, for what you committed has ruined you with Allah. When Yazid read the letter he said: Ibn Abbas was persistent in evil."
"10620","10591 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that Heraclius wrote to Mu'awiyah saying: If anything of prophethood remains among them, they shall inform me of what I ask them. He wrote asking about the Milky Way and the rainbow, and about the spot the sun struck only for one hour. When the letter and messenger came to Mu'awiyah, he said: This is something I never thought I would be asked about till today; who is for it? It was said: Ibn Abbas. Mu'awiyah folded Heraclius's letter and sent it to Ibn Abbas, and he wrote to him: The rainbow is safety for earth's people from drowning, the Milky Way is the gate of heaven from which it splits, and as for the spot the sun struck only for an hour of day, it is the sea parted for the Children of Israel."
"10621","10592 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated, my father narrated, he said: I heard Ya'la ibn Hakim narrating from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, I said to a man: Come, let us learn from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask them, for they are many. He said: Wonder, by Allah, at you, O Ibn Abbas; do you think people will need you while among people are whom you see of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I left that and turned to asking and following the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I would come to a man for a hadith that reached me that he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), find him napping, lay my cloak as pillow at his door with winds blowing dust on my face until he came out to me; when he saw me he said: O cousin of the Messenger of Allah, what is with you? I said: A hadith reached me that you narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I wished to hear it from you. He would say: Why did you not send to me that I come to you? I would say: I was more deserving to come to you. That man later saw me, when the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had gone and people needed me, saying: You were more deserving than I."
"10622","10593 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, he said: I sat with seventy or eighty persons of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); none of them opposed Ibn Abbas and met him but said: The saying is as you said, or said: You spoke truth."
"10623","10594 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated from dictation in his book in the year two hundred and twenty, Ubaydullah ibn Amr al-Raqqi narrated, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, Sa'id said: O Ibn Abbas, I find in the Qur'an things that confuse me and have entered my heart. Ibn Abbas said: Denial? The man said: Not denial, but confusion. Ibn Abbas said: Bring what is in your soul. The man said: I hear Allah say: There shall be no kinship among them that day nor shall they question one another, and He says in another verse: And they shall turn to one another questioning, and He says in another verse: Nor shall they hide any speech from Allah, and He says in another verse: By Allah our Lord, we were not polytheists - yet they hid in this verse. And in His saying: The heaven, He built it, raised its height and proportioned it, darkened its night and brought forth its morning, and after that He spread the earth - He mentions creation of heavens before earth, then says in another verse: Do you disbelieve in Him who created the earth in two days and set up equals to Him, that is Lord of worlds, and placed therein firm mountains above it and blessed it and measured its sustenance in four days, equal for seekers, then He rose to heaven while it was smoke and said to it and to earth: Come willingly or unwillingly; they said: We come willingly - He mentions creation of earth before heaven. And: And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful; And Allah is Mighty, Wise; And Allah is Hearing, Seeing - as if He was then passed. Ibn Abbas said: Bring what is in your soul. The questioner said: If you inform me of this, it suffices me. Ibn Abbas said: His saying: There shall be no kinship among them that day nor shall they question one another - this is at the first Blast, blown in the Trumpet: Whoever is in heavens and earth shall swoon except whom Allah wills; then there is no kinship nor questioning. Then at the second Blast they shall stand: And they turned to one another questioning. As for: By Allah our Lord, we were not polytheists, and: Nor shall they hide any speech from Allah - Allah on Resurrection Day forgives the sincere their sins, no sin is too great for Him to forgive, but He does not forgive shirk. When polytheists saw that, they said: Our Lord forgives sins but does not forgive shirk; so they said: We were people of sins but not polytheists. Then Allah said: Since you hid shirk, seal their mouths; so their mouths were sealed, their hands speak and their feet bear witness to what they earned. Then polytheists knew no speech is hidden from Allah; then: That day those who disbelieved and disobeyed the Messenger shall wish the earth leveled over them, nor shall they hide any speech from Allah. As for: The heaven, He built it to: And after that He spread the earth - He created earth in two days before heaven, then rose to heaven and proportioned them in another two days, then descended to earth and spread it - spreading it meaning bringing forth water and pasture, splitting rivers, making paths, creating mountains, sands, hills and what between them in another two days; that is: And after that He spread the earth. And: Do you disbelieve in Him who created the earth in two days to: In four days, equal for seekers - earth and what in it were made in four days, heavens in two days. As for: And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful, And Allah is Mighty, Wise, And Allah is Hearing, Seeing - Allah named Himself so, none other gave it to Him; And Allah is means He ever was so. Then he said to the man: Retain what I narrated to you, and know that what confuses you of the Qur'an is what I told you; Allah sent nothing but hitting thereby what He intended, but people do not know; let it not confuse you, for all is from Allah."
"10624","10595 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated, in the year two hundred and twenty-three, Hayyan ibn Ubaydullah ibn Zuhayr al-Misri Abu Zuhayr narrated sixty years ago, he said: I asked al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim about His saying: No calamity befalls in earth nor in yourselves but is in a Book before We bring it about; indeed that is easy for Allah, and about His saying: Indeed We used to transcribe what you did, and about His saying: Indeed We created everything with measure. He said: Ibn Abbas said: Allah created the Throne and rose over it, then created the Pen and commanded it to flow by His permission, and magnified the Pen as between heaven and earth. The Pen said: With what, my Lord, shall I flow? He said: With what I create and is in My creation: of rain, plant, soul or trace - meaning deed, provision or term. The Pen flowed with what shall be until Resurrection Day, and Allah affirmed it in the hidden Book with Him under the Throne. As for: Indeed We used to transcribe what you did - Allah appointed angels who transcribe from that Book each year in Ramadan - Laylat al-Qadr - what events shall be in earth until its like of the coming year; they compare it with Allah's guardian angels over servants every Thursday evening, and find what the guardians raised agrees with what is in their book, with neither addition nor omission. As for: Indeed We created everything with measure - Allah created for everything what suits it of His creation and what befits it of provision; He created the camel a creation suited to nothing else of animals, likewise all His creation; He created for land animals and birds provision suited to them on land, and for sea animals and birds provision suited to them in sea; that is: Indeed We created everything with measure."
"10625","10596 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Abu Razin, he said: Nafi' ibn al-Azraq disputed with Ibn Abbas saying: Do you find the five prayers in Allah's Book? He said: Yes. He recited to him: Glory be to Allah when you enter evening - Maghrib; And when you enter morning - Subh; And in the afternoon - Asr; And when you enter midday - he said: Zuhr; And after the Isha prayer - he said: Isha prayer."
"10626","10597 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Harrani - and he is Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tara'ifi - narrated, Ubaydullah ibn Ayyash and Musa ibn Yazid al-Harraniyyayn narrated, they said: Juwaybir narrated, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim al-Hilali, he said: Nafi' ibn al-Azraq and Najdah ibn Uwaymir went out with a group of Kharijite chiefs to probe knowledge and seek it, until they came to Mecca, and there was Abdullah ibn Abbas sitting near Zamzam, wearing a red cloak and shirt, with people standing asking him about tafsir, saying: O Ibn Abbas, what do you say about such and such? And he would say: It is such and such. Nafi' ibn al-Azraq said to him: How bold you are, O Ibn Abbas, upon what you venture since today. Ibn Abbas said to him: May your mother lose you, O Nafi', tell me who is bolder than I? He said: Who is he, O Ibn Abbas? He said: A man who speaks of what he has no knowledge of, and a man who conceals knowledge he has. He said: You spoke truth, O Ibn Abbas; I came to ask you. He said: Bring, O Ibn al-Azraq, ask. He said: Inform me about Allah's saying: There shall be sent against you a flame of fire - what is shuwaz? He said: Flame with no smoke in it. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about His saying: And smoke, so you shall not prevail - what is nuhas? He said: Smoke with no flame in it. He said: Did Arabs know that? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Nabighah of Banu Dhubyan. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: Mingled, that We may test him - He said: The man's water and woman's water when gathered in the womb become mashj. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Abu Dhu'ayb al-Hudhali. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: And the leg is joined with the leg - what is leg with leg? He said: War. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Abu Dhu'ayb. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: Sons and grandsons - what are sons and grandsons? He said: Your sons, for they help you; as for your grandsons, they are your servants. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt al-Thaqafi. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: You are only of the bewitched - who are the bewitched? He said: Of the created. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt. He said: You spoke truth; inform us about Allah's saying: But We cast them into the sea while he was blameworthy - what is mulim? He said: Sinful. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: Say, I seek refuge with the Lord of daybreak - what is falaq? He said: Morning light. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Labid ibn Rabi'ah. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: That you may not grieve over what escaped you nor rejoice in what came to you - what is grief? He said: That you not sorrow. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Labid ibn Rabi'ah. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: He thought he would never return - what is yahur? He said: Return. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Labid ibn Rabi'ah. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: Circling between it and intensely hot water - what is an? He said: That whose heat reached utmost. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Nabighah of Banu Dhubyan. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: And it became as darkness - what is sarim? He said: Like the dark night. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Nabighah of Banu Dhubyan. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: To the darkness of night - what is ghasaq of night? He said: When it darkens. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of al-Nabighah. Abu Khalifah said: The poetry verses cited here are omitted in the print. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: And Allah is over all things Powerful - what is muqit? He said: Able. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of al-Nabighah. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: And the night when it approaches - He said: Its coming with its blackness. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Imru' al-Qays. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: And I am responsible for it - He said: The guarantor is the surety. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Imru' al-Qays. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: And its wheat - what is fum? He said: Wheat. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Abu Dhu'ayb al-Hudhali. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: Azlam - what is azlam? He said: Divining arrows. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of al-Hutay'ah. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: Companions of the left - who are companions of the left? He said: Companions of the left hand. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Did you not hear the saying of Zuhayr ibn Abi Sulma. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: And when the seas are mixed - He said: Its water mixes with earth's water. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Zuhayr ibn Abi Sulma. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: And the heaven full of paths - what is hubuk? He said: Full of ways. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Zuhayr ibn Abi Sulma. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: Exalted is the greatness of our Lord - what is His greatness? He said: His might is exalted. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Tarafah ibn al-Abd to al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: Until he becomes wasted - He said: Harad is the worn out. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Tarafah ibn al-Abd. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: While you are heedless - what is samidun? He said: Amused. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Huzaylah bint Bakr while weeping for Ad. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: When it gathers - what is its gathering? He said: When it joins. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Ibn Sirmah al-Ansari. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: The One, the Eternal - as for the One we know, what is Samad? He said: The One to whom all matters are turned. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of al-Asadiyyah. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: He shall meet punishment - what is atham? He said: Recompense. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Bishr ibn Abi Hazim al-Asadi. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: While he is suppressed with grief - what is kazim? He said: Silent. He said: Did Arabs know that? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Zuhayr ibn Jadhimah al-Absi. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: Or you hear for them any sound - He said: A sound. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Khidash ibn Zuhayr. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: When you slew them by His permission - He said: When you killed them by His permission. He said: Did Arabs know that before the Book came down to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; did you not hear the saying of Utbah al-Laythi. He said: You spoke truth; inform me about Allah's saying: O Prophet, when you divorce women - was there divorce in pre-Islam? He said: Yes, an irrevocable triple divorce; did you not hear the saying of A'sha of Banu Qays ibn Tha'labah when his wife's brothers of Anazah seized him and said to him: You harmed our companion, and we swear by Allah we shall not lift the stick from you until you divorce her; when he saw their seriousness and that they would do him harm, he said verses divorcing her thrice. They said: By Allah you shall make the divorce clear, or we shall not lift the stick; and he said verses; they said: By Allah you shall make the divorce clear; and he said verses; so he separated her with three divorces."
"10627","10598 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, (Ha) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated, both from Ikrimah ibn Ammar, Abu Zumayl al-Hanafi narrated, Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated, he said: When Harura' seceded, dwelling alone in a land, I said to Ali: O Commander of the Faithful, delay from prayer; perhaps I may come to these people and speak to them. He said: I fear them for you. I said: No, Allah willing. He said: I wore the best Yemeni clothes I could, then entered upon them while they were napping at midday; I entered upon people never seeing people more striving than them, their hands like camels' calluses, their faces marked from prostration. I entered and they said: Welcome, O Ibn Abbas, what brings you? He said: I came to narrate to you from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); revelation came down while they are most knowing of its interpretation. Some said: Do not narrate to him, and some said: We shall narrate to him. He said: I said: Inform me what you hold against the cousin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his son-in-law, the first to believe in him, while the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are with him? They said: We hold three things against him. I said: What are they? They said: First, he appointed men as judges in Allah's religion, while Allah said: Judgment belongs only to Allah. I said: And what else? They said: He fought but did not take captives nor booty; if they were disbelievers, their wealth was lawful to him, and if they were believers, their blood was forbidden to him. I said: And what else? They said: He erased himself from Commander of the Faithful; if he is not Commander of the Faithful, he is commander of disbelievers. I said: What if I recite to you from Allah's decisive Book and narrate to you from your Prophet's Sunnah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what you cannot deny - will you return? They said: Yes. He said: I said: As for your saying he appointed men in Allah's religion, He says: O you who believe, do not kill game while in ihram to His saying: Two just men among you shall judge it, and He said about a woman and her husband: If you fear breach between them, send an arbiter from his family and an arbiter from hers. I adjure you by Allah, is men's judgment in sparing their blood and selves and mending relations more deserving, or regarding a rabbit worth a quarter dirham? They said: O Allah, regarding sparing their blood and mending relations. He said: Have I resolved this? They said: O Allah, yes. As for your saying he fought but did not take captives nor booty - would you take your mother captive, or deem lawful from her what you deem lawful from others, for then you disbelieved? And if you claim she is not your mother, you disbelieved and left Islam; Allah says: The Prophet is closer to the believers than themselves, and his wives are their mothers. You waver between two misguidances; choose whichever you wish. Have I resolved this? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: As for your saying he erased himself from Commander of the Faithful - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Quraysh on Hudaybiyah day to write a document between him and them, saying: Write: This is what Muhammad the Messenger of Allah agreed upon. They said: By Allah, had we known you are Allah's Messenger we would not have barred you from the House nor fought you, but write: Muhammad ibn Abdullah. He said: By Allah I am Allah's Messenger though you deny me; write, O Ali, Muhammad ibn Abdullah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was better than Ali. Have I resolved this? They said: O Allah, yes. Then twenty thousand of them returned, and four thousand remained, and were killed."
"10628","10599 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, he said: Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When you come to an awesome ruler fearing he may assault you, say: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest above all His creation; Allah is Mightier than what I fear and dread; I seek refuge with Allah besides whom there is no god, who holds the seven heavens lest they fall upon earth but by His permission, from the evil of Your servant so-and-so and his troops and followers of jinn and men; my God, be for me a protector from their evil; exalted is Your praise, mighty is Your protection, blessed is Your name, there is no god but You - three times."
"10629","10600 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: Ibn Abbas used to say: O Allah, I ask You by the light of Your Face by which heavens and earth shone, to place me in Your refuge, Your protection, Your neighborhood, and under Your shelter."
"10630","10601 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated, from Hajjaj, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Do you know what you did and what you gave fatwa about? Riders carried your fatwa, and poets spoke of it. He said: And what did they say? I said: They said verses. He said: To Allah we belong and to Him we return; by Allah I did not give fatwa so, nor intended this, nor permitted of it but what Allah permitted of dead meat, blood and pork."
"10631","10602 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Mis'ar narrated, from Abu Rashid, freedman of Banu Amir, he said: I saw on the bed of Ibn Abbas, or in the gathering of Ibn Abbas, a cushion of khazz (silk-wool)."
"10632","10603 - Ali narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Salamah ibn Nubayt al-Ashja'i narrated, al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim narrated, he said: Ibn Abbas passed a storyteller and kicked him with his foot, saying: Do you know the abrogating from the abrogated? He said: And what is abrogating from abrogated? He said: You do not know abrogating from abrogated? He said: No. He said: You perished and caused ruin."
"10633","10604 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated, from Atiyyah, he said: A young man asked Ibn Abbas: May one kiss while fasting? He said: No. Then an old man came and said: May one kiss while fasting? He said: Yes. The young man said: I asked you: may I kiss while fasting, and you said: No; and this one asked you: may he kiss while fasting, and you said: Yes; how is lawful for him what is forbidden for me, while we are upon one religion? Ibn Abbas said to him: The veins of the testicles are attached to the nose; when the nose smells, the organ moves, and when it moves it calls to what is greater; and the old man controls his desire. That was after Abdullah's sight had gone, and behind him was a woman; it was said: O Ibn Abbas, behind you is a woman. He said: Fie upon you, an evil sitter with people."
"10634","10605 - Ali narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Abdullah ibn al-Walid al-Ijli narrated, Bukayr ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I would wish I had a man of qadar before me that I strike his head. They said: Why? He said: For Allah created a preserved Tablet of white pearl, its covers of red ruby, its pen light, its writing light, its width as between heaven and earth; He looks into it three hundred and sixty times each day; with each look He creates, gives life and death, honors and humbles, and does what He wills."
"10635","10606 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, Mus'ab ibn Sawwar narrated, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: When Allah sent Musa, peace be upon him, and revealed the Torah to him, he said: O Allah, You are a great Lord; had You wished to be obeyed You would have been obeyed, and had You wished not to be disobeyed You would not have been disobeyed; yet You love to be obeyed while You are disobeyed - how is this, my Lord? Allah revealed to him: I am not questioned about what I do, but they shall be questioned. Musa, peace be upon him, desisted. When Allah sent Uzayr and revealed the Torah to him after it had been lifted from the Children of Israel, until some said he is son of Allah, he said: O Allah, You are a great Lord; had You wished to be obeyed You would have been obeyed, and had You wished not to be disobeyed You would not have been disobeyed; yet You love to be obeyed while You are disobeyed - how, my Lord? Allah revealed to him: I am not questioned about what I do, but they shall be questioned. His soul refused till he asked again, saying: O Allah, You are a great Lord; had You wished not to be disobeyed You would not have been disobeyed, yet You love to be obeyed while You are disobeyed - how is this, my Lord? Allah revealed to him: I am not questioned about what I do, but they shall be questioned. His soul refused till he asked again, saying: Can you gather a purse of sun? He said: No. He said: Can you bring a measure of wind? He said: No. He said: Can you bring a weight of light? He said: No. Can you bring a carat of light? He said: No. He said: Likewise you cannot bear what you asked about; I am not questioned about what I do, but they shall be questioned. I shall make your punishment only that I erase your name from the prophets so you are not mentioned among them. So He erased his name from the prophets, and he is not mentioned among them though he is a prophet. When Allah sent Isa, peace be upon him, and he saw his station with his Lord, and He taught him the Book, wisdom, Torah and Gospel, and he healed the blind and leper, gave life to dead, and informed them of what they eat and store in houses, he said: O Allah, You are a great Lord; had You wished to be obeyed You would have been obeyed, and had You wished not to be disobeyed You would not have been disobeyed; yet You love to be obeyed while You are disobeyed - how is this, my Lord? Allah revealed to him: I am not questioned about what I do, but they shall be questioned; you are My servant and Messenger, My word cast to Maryam, and a spirit from Me; I created you from dust then said to you: Be, and you were. If you do not desist I shall do with you as I did with your companion before you; I am not questioned about what I do, but they shall be questioned. Isa, peace be upon him, gathered his followers saying: Qadar is Allah's secret, so do not burden yourselves with it."
"10636","10607 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, Yazid ibn Abi Salamah Abu Yusuf narrated, he said: I heard Wahb ibn Munabbih say: I accompanied Ibn Abbas before his sight was afflicted and after it was afflicted; he was asked about qadar, saying: I found the soundest of people in speech about it the most ignorant of it, and the weakest in speech about it the most knowing of it; and I found one who looks into it like one who looks into sunbeams - the more he looks the more his sight is perplexed."
"10637","10608 - Ali narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Abdullah ibn al-Walid al-Ijli narrated, from Bukayr ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Mosques are Allah's houses on earth; they shine for heaven's people as heaven's stars shine for earth's people."
"10638","10609 - Ali narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Dirar ibn Murrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Had Pharaoh said to me: May Allah bless you, I would say: And you - though Pharaoh has died."
"10639","10610 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abd al-Mu'min Abu Ubayd narrated, Mahdi ibn Mahdi narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: No year comes upon people but they innovate therein a bid'ah and kill therein a sunnah, until bid'ahs live and sunan die."
"10640","10611 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from his father, that Ibn Abbas used to take a seed of pomegranate and eat it. It was said to him: O Ibn Abbas, why do you do this? He said: It reached me that there is no pomegranate on earth pollinated but with a seed of Paradise's seeds; perhaps it is this."
"10641","10612 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Ibn al-Adhra narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Whoever wears yellow sandals remains in joy as long as he wears them."
"10642","10613 - Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Adhani narrated to us, Abu Umayr ibn al-Nahhas narrated, Damrah ibn Rabi'ah narrated, from Ibn Shawdhab, from Matar al-Warraq, from Zahdam al-Jarmi, he said: We were in Ibn Abbas's evening gathering, and he said: I shall narrate to you a hadith neither secret nor public: when there happened of this man's affair what happened - meaning Uthman - I said to Ali: Withdraw; had you been in a hole you would be sought till taken out. He disobeyed me. By Allah, Mu'awiyah shall surely rule over you, for Allah says: Whoever is killed unjustly, We gave his heir authority, so let him not exceed in killing; indeed he is aided. Quraysh shall surely carry you upon the way of Persia and Rome, and Christians, Jews and Magians shall claim favor over you. Whoever of you that day holds to what he knows shall be saved, and whoever abandons - and you shall abandon - you shall be as a generation among generations of those perished."
"10643","10614 - Ali ibn al-Abbas al-Bajali al-Kufi narrated to us, Muqaddam ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated, my uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that he was in Maymunah's house and placed purification water for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who placed it? Ibn Abbas said: I. He struck my shoulder saying: O Allah, give him understanding in religion and teach him interpretation."
"10644","10615 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated, Yahya ibn Adam narrated, from Abu Kudaynah Yahya ibn al-Muhallab, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw Jibril twice, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated wisdom for me twice."
"10645","10616 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shu'bah informed, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Umar would question me along with the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said to him: You question him? He said: He is from where you know. He asked them about: When Allah's help and victory come; I said: It is only the term of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and recited the surah to its end to: He is Ever-Relenting. Umar said: You spoke truth."
"10646","10617 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Umar would admit me with the elders of Badr; some of them said: Why do you admit this youth with us while we have sons like him? He said: He is of whom you know. He said: He invited them one day and invited me, and I saw he invited me that day only to show them of me. He said: What do you say about: When Allah's help and victory come, and you see people entering Allah's religion in crowds, until he sealed the surah. Some said: We are commanded to praise Allah and seek His forgiveness when we are aided and conquest comes to us. Some said: We do not know, and some said nothing. He said to me: O Ibn Abbas, do you say likewise? I said: No. He said: What do you say? I said: It is the term of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Allah informed him: when Allah's help comes, and victory - the victory of Mecca - that is the sign of your term: So glorify the praises of your Lord and seek His forgiveness; indeed He is Ever-Relenting. Umar said: I know of it only what you know."
"10647","10618 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed, Ma'mar informed, from Qatadah and Asim, that they heard Ikrimah say: Ibn Abbas said: Umar ibn al-Khattab called the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked them about Laylat al-Qadr; they agreed it is in the last ten. Ibn Abbas said: I said to Umar: I know and I think which night it is. Umar said: Which night is it? I said: The seventh that passes, or the seventh that remains, of the last ten. Umar said: From where did you know that? Ibn Abbas said: I said: Allah created seven heavens, seven earths and seven days; the month turns in seven; man is created from seven, eats from seven, prostrates upon seven; tawaf of the House is seven, and stoning the jamarat is seven - for things he mentioned. Umar said: You discerned a matter we did not discern. Qatadah would add from Ibn Abbas in his saying: eats from seven, he said: It is Allah's saying: Then We caused to grow therein grain, and grapes and herbage, the verse."
"10648","10619 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, Abu Usamah Hammad ibn Usamah narrated, Mujalid narrated to me, Amir al-Sha'bi informed, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Al-Abbas said to me: Dear son, the Commander of the Faithful invites you, draws you near and consults you with the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so retain from me three traits: beware lest he try a lie upon you, never disclose his secret, and never backbite anyone with him. Amir said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Each one is better than ten thousand."
"10649","10620 - Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, he said: I entered upon al-Hasan and he said: Ibn Abbas was of a station with the Qur'an; Umar used to say: That is the youth of the elders; he has an asking tongue and an understanding heart. He would stand - I think he said - upon this minbar of ours on the evening of Arafah, recite Surah al-Baqarah and Surah Al Imran, then explain them verse by verse; and he was a copious, generous, abundant spring."
"10650","10621 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, from Kahmas ibn al-Hasan, from Ibn Buraydah al-Aslami, he said: A man reviled Ibn Abbas, and Ibn Abbas said: You revile me while in me are three traits: when I come upon a verse of Allah's Book, I wish all people knew of it what I know; when I hear of a Muslim judge judging justly I rejoice for him, though I may never litigate to him; and when I hear of rain striking a Muslim land I rejoice, though I have no grazing livestock in it."
"10651","10622 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbadah al-Wasiti narrated, Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Amr ibn Maymun, from his father, he said: When Ibn Abbas's sight was taken, he would say to his guide: When you bring me to Mu'awiyah, direct me to his bed, then release my hand lest Mu'awiyah gloat over me. He did so one day, and Mu'awiyah said to one of his sitters: He shall surely grieve. When he sat with him on his bed he said: O Ibn Abbas, may Allah reward you in al-Hasan ibn Ali. He said: Did he die? He said: Yes. He said: Allah's mercy and pleasure upon him, and join him with his righteous predecessors. By Allah, O Mu'awiyah, he shall not fill your pit, nor eat his provision, nor remain immortal after him; and we were afflicted with a greater loss than him: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), yet Allah did not forsake us after him."
"10652","And what Abdullah ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, transmitted with chain. Abdullah ibn Umar from Ibn Abbas. 10623 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari and Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, they said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: When Umar was stabbed, Ibn Abbas said to him: O Commander of the Faithful, may Allah reward you with good; rejoice, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for you that Allah honor the religion through you, while people disagreed. When you embraced Islam, your Islam was honor; Allah manifested Islam, His Messenger and his Companions through you; you emigrated to Medina, and your emigration was a victory; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while pleased with you."
"10653","Abu al-Tufayl from Ibn Abbas. 10624 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated, Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Numayri narrated, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr and Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Mecca: How pleasant and beloved you are to me; had your people not expelled me from you, I would not have dwelt elsewhere."
"10654","10625 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, (Ha) and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khallad ibn Yahya narrated, they said: Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated, from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: Ibn Abbas entered upon me, and I said: O Abu Abbas - or: O Ibn Abbas - your people claim the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed raml and that it is sunnah. He said: They spoke truth and lied; he did perform raml, but it is not sunnah. Rather the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions came while the polytheists were upon Mount Qu'ayqi'an; it reached him they say: He and his Companions are emaciated. So he commanded them to perform raml to show them he has strength."
"10655","10626 - Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Fitr, from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas, and he mentioned the like."
"10656","10627 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, (Ha) and Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, they said: Sufyan narrated, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Husayn, from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Your people claim the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed raml at the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and that it is sunnah. He said: They spoke truth and lied; it is not sunnah."
"10657","10628 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abu Ghanim al-Ghanawi, from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Your people claim the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed raml at the House, and that it is sunnah. He said: They spoke truth and lied. I said: In what did they speak truth, and in what did they lie? He said: They spoke truth that he performed raml, and lied that it is sunnah. Quraysh said: Leave Muhammad and his Companions from Hudaybiyah till they die the death of naghaf (worms). When they reconciled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that they come the next year and stay in Mecca three days, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came the next year while the polytheists were toward Qu'ayqi'an. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: Perform raml at the House - and it is not sunnah. I said: Your people claim the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated between al-Safa and al-Marwah upon a camel, and that it is sunnah. He said: They spoke truth and lied. I said: In what did they speak truth, and in what did they lie? He said: They spoke truth, he did circumambulate upon a camel, and lied that it is sunnah; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not push people from himself nor have them struck from him, so he circumambulated upon a camel that they hear his speech, see his place, and their hands not reach him. I said: Your people claim the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ran between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and that it is sunnah. He said: They spoke truth; Ibrahim, peace be upon him, when commanded with the rites, Satan confronted him at the course, so he raced him and Ibrahim, peace be upon him, outran him. Then Jibril, peace be upon him, took him to Jamrat al-Aqabah; Satan confronted him, and he stoned him with seven pebbles till he left. He confronted at the middle jamrah, and he stoned him with seven till he left. Then he laid him upon the forehead, while upon Isma'il was a white shirt; he said to him: Father, there is no shirt, so shroud me in it. Ibrahim, peace be upon him, turned, and there was a large-eyed, white, horned ram; he slaughtered it there. Then Jibril, peace be upon him, took him to the farthest jamrah; Satan confronted him, and he stoned him with seven till he left. Then he took him to Mina saying: This is the Sacred Monument. Then he took him to Arafah. Ibn Abbas said: Do you know why Arafah was named Arafah? I said: Why was Arafah named? He said: Jibril, peace be upon him, said: Did you know? He said: Yes. Then Ibn Abbas said: Do you know how the talbiyah was? I said: And how was the talbiyah? He said: When Ibrahim, peace be upon him, was commanded to call people to hajj, mountains lowered their heads for him, villages were raised for him, and he called among people."
"10658","10629 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abd al-Karim, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered Mecca, said: The people claimed you perished in emaciation and hunger; so perform raml when you enter and touch, three circuits. They did, and Mecca's people said: We see the people but strong, though you claimed they perished in emaciation."
"10659","10630 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed umrah from al-Ji'ranah and circumambulated the House walking."
"10660","10631 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed, Ma'mar and al-Thawri informed, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas and Mu'awiyah while they circumambulated the House; Mu'awiyah would pass no corner but touched it. Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would touch only the Yemeni corner. Mu'awiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Nothing of the House is abandoned."
"10661","10632 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, (Ha) and Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, they said: Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated, Abu al-Tufayl narrated to me, that he saw Mu'awiyah circumambulating the Ka'bah, at his left Abdullah ibn Abbas, while I followed behind them hearing their speech. Mu'awiyah began touching the two corners of the Stone, and Ibn Abbas would say to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not touch these two corners. Mu'awiyah would say: Leave me, O Ibn Abbas, for nothing of it is abandoned."
"10662","10633 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated, Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr and Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Mecca: How pleasant and beloved you are to me; had my people not expelled me from you, I would not have dwelt elsewhere."
"10663","10634 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: Mu'awiyah and Ibn Abbas performed hajj; Mu'awiyah began touching all the corners. Ibn Abbas said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touch only these two corners."
"10664","10635 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi' al-Tahhan al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, (Ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated, they said: Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Tufayl al-Bakri, that he narrated to him, that he heard Ibn Abbas say: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touch other than the two Yemeni corners."
"10665","10636 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: Mu'awiyah performed hajj and would come to no corner of the House but touched it. Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would touch only the Yemeni corner and the Stone. Mu'awiyah said: None of the House's corners is abandoned."
"10666","10637 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ibn Khuthaym, or from al-Ala' - Abu Bakr doubted - from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard him say: We used to call it Shuba'ah, meaning Zamzam, and we found it a good help for dependents."
"10667","10638 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated, from Qatadah, from Anas, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought people of al-Zutt worshipping an idol, and he burned them with fire. Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said: Whoever changes his religion, kill him."
"10668","Tha'labah ibn al-Hakam from Ibn Abbas. 10639 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated, (Ha) and Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated, they said: Amr ibn Hammad narrated, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Tha'labah ibn al-Hakam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: People plundered sheep and slaughtered them, then began cooking. The Messenger of Allah came and ordered the pots overturned, saying: Plunder is not lawful."
"10669","Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah from his father. 10640 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed, Abu Ibrahim al-Madani Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated, he said: I entered upon Amrah bint Ubaydullah ibn Abbas; she said: I heard from my father, saying: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any believer who frees a believer, Allah frees for each of his limbs a limb of him from the Fire. Thus al-Nadr narrated it, from Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd, from Amrah bint Ubaydullah ibn al-Abbas; and Abu Amir al-Aqadi opposed him, saying: From Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas."
"10670","10641 - Muhammad ibn Salih al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated, Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated, from Amrah bint Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Abbas, from her father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frees a believer in this world, Allah frees for each of his limbs a limb of him from the Fire."
"10671","10642 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Abu Jahdam Musa ibn Salim, Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated to me, he said: We sat with Ibn Abbas among youths of Banu Hashim, and a man asked him: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Zuhr and Asr? He said: No. He said: Perhaps he recited to himself. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a servant commanded with a command and conveyed; by Allah he singled us out with nothing apart from people but three: he commanded us to perfect wudu, commanded us not to eat charity, and not to mate donkeys upon horses."
"10672","10643 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Waki' narrated, from Sufyan, from Abu Jahdam, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to perfect wudu."
"10673","Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf from Ibn Abbas. 10644 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Qirmiti narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah al-Talhi al-Madani narrated, my father Abdullah ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Abd al-Majid ibn Suhayl, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: A rabbit was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while A'ishah slept; he set aside for her of it the rump. When she awoke he gave it to her and she ate it."
"10674","Kathir ibn al-Abbas from Abdullah ibn al-Abbas. 10645 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Kathir ibn al-Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed on the day the sun eclipsed four bowings in two rak'ahs and four prostrations."
"10675","Shahr ibn Hawshab from Ibn Abbas. 10646 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to me, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, he said: Ibn Abbas said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat in his house's courtyard in Mecca, Uthman ibn Maz'un passed him and smiled to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do not sit. He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah sat facing him; while he spoke to him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed his gaze to heaven, looked a while to heaven, then lowered his gaze where he placed it to his right on earth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned from his sitter Uthman to where he placed his gaze, shaking his head as seeking to understand what is said to him, while Ibn Maz'un watched. When he finished his need and understood what is said, the Messenger of Allah fixed his gaze till it vanished in heaven, then turned to Uthman in his first sitting. He said: O Muhammad, in what did I sit with you? I never saw you do as you did this morning. He said: Did you notice that? Uthman said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah's messenger, peace be upon him, came to me while you sat? He said: Yes. What did he say to you? He said: Indeed Allah commands justice, excellence and giving kin, and forbids indecency, evil and transgression; He admonishes you that you may remember. Uthman said: Then faith settled in my heart, and I loved Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10676","Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas from his father. 10647 - Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Missisi narrated to us, Abu Umayr ibn al-Nahhas narrated, Damrah narrated, from Ali ibn Abi Hamalah and al-Awza'i, they said: Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas would prostrate a thousand prostrations each day."
"10677","10648 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated, al-Minhal ibn Amr narrated, Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated, from his father, he said: Al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib commanded me, saying: Spend the night with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I went to the mosque; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led people in the last Isha prayer until none remained in the mosque but him. He said: Then he passed by me saying: Who is this? I said: Abdullah. He said: What then? I said: Al-Abbas commanded me to spend tonight with you. He said: Then join. When he left, he entered saying: Spread for Abdullah. A cushion of sackcloth was brought to me. Al-Abbas had charged me: Do not sleep till you observe his prayer. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came forward and slept till I heard his snoring; then he sat upright on his bed, raised his head to heaven saying: Glory be to the Sovereign, the Holy, three times. Then he recited this verse from the end of Surah Al Imran till he sealed it: Indeed in the creation of heavens and earth. Then he stood, brushed with his siwak, performed wudu, entered his prayer place and prayed two rak'ahs neither short nor long. Then he returned to his bed and slept till I heard his snoring; then he sat upright and did as the first time, then brushed, performed wudu, entered his prayer place and prayed two rak'ahs neither long nor short. Then he returned to his bed and slept till I heard his snoring; then he sat upright and did as he did, prayed then performed witr. When he finished his prayer I heard him say: O Allah, place light in my sight, light in my hearing, light in my tongue, light in my heart, light on my right, light on my left, light before me, light behind me, light above me, light below me, light for me on Resurrection Day, and magnify light for me."
"10678","10649 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, Dawud ibn Isa al-Nakha'i narrated to me, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated to me, my father narrated to me, that his father sent him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a need. He said: I found him sitting with his Companions in the mosque, and could not speak to him. When he prayed Maghrib he stood praying voluntary till the caller called for Isha, people returned, then he prayed the prayer and stood praying, till those remaining in the mosque left. Then he left for his house, and I followed him. When he heard my step he said: Who is this? And turned to me. I said: Ibn Abbas. He said: The cousin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: The cousin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Welcome to the cousin of the Messenger of Allah; what brings you? I said: My father sent me for such and such. He said: Did you just come? I said: No. He said: Since you did not leave till this hour, you shall not leave. He entered his house and I entered with him. I said: I shall observe the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He slept till I heard his snoring, then awoke, cast his gaze to heaven, recited these verses in Surah Al Imran: Indeed in the creation of heavens and earth, to the end, the five verses, till he ended at: Indeed You never break the promise. Then he said: O Allah, place light in my hearing, light in my sight, light beneath me, place for me with You light. Beside him was a wash-basin of brass covered, with a siwak upon it; he brushed, performed wudu, prayed two rak'ahs, returned and slept again till I heard his snoring. Then he awoke, recited the verses, supplicated the supplication, brushed, performed wudu, prayed two rak'ahs. Then he slept till I heard his snoring. Then he awoke, recited the verses, supplicated, brushed, performed wudu, prayed two rak'ahs. Then he slept till I heard his snoring; he recited the verses, supplicated, brushed, performed wudu, then prayed a prayer I knew he performed witr in. I came to his left side; he took my ear with his finger and turned me till he placed me at his right side. Then he prayed two rak'ahs of Fajr, then went out to prayer."
"10679","10650 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti narrated, he said: I heard al-Awza'i, from Isma'il ibn Ubaydullah al-Makhzumi, from Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father Abdullah ibn Abbas, he said: There was shown to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what shall be opened for his ummah after him, land after land, and he rejoiced at that. Then Allah revealed: And your Lord shall surely give you, and you shall be pleased. Allah gave him in Paradise a thousand palaces, in each palace what befits him of youths and servants."
"10680","10651 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, he said: Al-Mahdi led us in prayer and recited aloud: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. I spoke to him about that, and he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite aloud: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate."
"10681","10652 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to me, my father narrated to me, from his father, he said: Al-Mahdi wrote to me of my covenant and commanded me to be firm in judgment, saying in his letter: My father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord said: By My might and majesty, I shall surely avenge the wrongdoer in his present and future, and I shall avenge whoever saw a wronged one, could help him, and did not."
"10682","10653 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Musarrif ibn Amr al-Yami narrated, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated, from Husayn, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Prophet woke at night he brushed, then performed wudu and recited: Indeed in the alternation of night and day, to the end of the two verses. Then he stood and prayed two rak'ahs, then left and slept till he breathed in sleep. Then he stood and did the like, then came to his bed, then stood and prayed two rak'ahs, then did likewise as the first time, then performed witr with three."
"10683","10654 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, al-Walid ibn Uqbah narrated, from Hamzah al-Zayyat, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly, but he did not say: from his father."
"10684","10655 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Hilal narrated, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray by day two by two."
"10685","10656 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to me, Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim narrated, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, from Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered on the day of the Conquest, while upon the Ka'bah were three hundred and sixty idols; Iblis had fastened their feet with lead. He came with his staff, began pointing it at each idol and it fell upon its face, saying: Truth has come and falsehood has perished; indeed falsehood is ever perishing. Till he passed over them all."
"10686","10657 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, and Hisham ibn Urwah, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a shoulder or meat, then prayed without rinsing and without touching water."
"10687","10658 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a limb and prayed without performing wudu."
"10688","10659 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate in the house of Duba'ah bint al-Harith a shoulder of meat with broth, then prayed without touching water."
"10689","10660 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated, Ibn Thawban narrated, from Dawud ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate meat and prayed without performing wudu."
"10690","10661 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate in the house of Duba'ah bint al-Harith a shoulder."
"10691","10662 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, (Ha) and al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abdah ibn Abdullah al-Saffar narrated, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a shoulder, then went out to prayer without renewing wudu."
"10692","10663 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah informed, (Ha) and Ishaq ibn Khalawayh al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated, from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Hanzali, from Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, that he saw Allah's Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat of a roasted shoulder, then pray, without performing wudu from that."
"10693","10664 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to me, Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated, Abdullah ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali informed, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Abbas, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Love Allah for what He nourishes you with of His blessings, love me for Allah's love, and love my household for my love."
"10694","10665 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Ja'far al-Ramli narrated, (Ha) and Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, they said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, he said: al-Hakam ibn Mus'ab narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever adheres to istighfar, Allah shall make for him relief from every worry, exit from every strait, and provide him whence he does not expect."
"10695","10666 - Al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Hashim al-Tusi narrated, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated, from Utbah ibn Yaqzan, from Dawud ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is created oft-tried, oft-repenting, oft-forgetting; when reminded, he remembers."
"10696","10667 - Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated, Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Marwadhi narrated, from Sulayman ibn Qarm, from Muhammad ibn Sa'id, from Dawud ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A bird was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You. Ali came, and he said: O Allah, and to me."
"10697","10668 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Dawud ibn Ali, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, he said: Al-Abbas sent me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I came to him in the evening while he was in the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood praying at night; when he prayed the two rak'ahs before Fajr he said: O Allah, I ask You for mercy from You by which You guide my heart, gather my dispersion, mend my disarray, restore my affection, set right my religion, guard my absent, raise my present, purify my deed, whiten my face, inspire my rectitude, and protect me from every evil. O Allah, grant me true faith, certainty after which is no disbelief, and mercy by which I attain the honor of Your nobility in this world and the next. O Allah, I ask You success at decree, the abode of martyrs, life of the felicitous, companionship of prophets, and victory over enemies. O Allah, I laid my need before You; though my view falls short, my deed is weak, and I need Your mercy; I ask You, O Decider of matters, O Healer of breasts, as You separate between seas, to shelter me from the torment of Blaze, the call of perdition, and the trial of graves. O Allah, whatever my view falls short of, my deed is weak for, and my wish does not reach, of good You promised any of Your servants, or good You shall give any of Your creation - I desire it of You and ask You, O Lord of worlds. O Allah, make us guides, guided, neither straying nor misleading, war to Your enemies and peace to Your allies; we love people by Your love, and oppose by Your enmity whoever of Your creation opposes You. O Allah, this is the supplication, and upon You is the response. O Allah, this is the effort, and upon You is reliance; there is no power nor strength but with Allah. O Allah, Possessor of the strong rope and wise command, I ask You safety on the Day of Threat, and Paradise on the Day of Eternity, with the near, witnessing, bowing, prostrating, covenant-fulfilling; indeed You are Merciful, Loving, and You do what You will. Glory to Him who wrapped might and spoke thereby; glory to Him whom praise befits but Him; glory to the Possessor of Throne and splendor; glory to the Possessor of power and generosity; glory to Him who encompassed all things with His knowledge. O Allah, place for me light in my heart, light in my grave, light in my hearing, light in my sight, light in my hair, light in my skin, light in my flesh, light in my blood, light in my bones, light before me, light behind me, light on my right, light on my left, light above me, light beneath me. O Allah, increase me in light, magnify light for me, and make light for me."
"10698","10669 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Yahya ibn al-Ala, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Dawud ibn Ali, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hang the whip where the household see it."
"10699","10670 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from Dawud ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hang the whip where the household see it."
"10700","10671 - Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Dimashqi narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal narrated, Sallam ibn Sulayman narrated, Isa and Abd al-Samad, sons of Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, narrated, from their father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hang the whip where the household see it, for it disciplines them."
"10701","10672 - Ahmad ibn Mas'ud al-Maqdisi narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated, Mindal ibn Ali narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Dawud ibn Ali, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hang your whip where your family see it."
"10702","10673 - Ubayd ibn Muhammad ibn Subayh al-Zayyat al-Kufi narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, my father narrated, from Isa ibn al-Mukhtar, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Dawud ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed for rain saying: O Allah, give us relieving, fertile, covering, prompt rain without delay, beneficial without harm. We had not waited but we were rained upon till everything flowed; they came to him saying: We drowned. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, around us, not upon us."
"10703","10674 - Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt al-Kufi narrated, Mindal ibn Ali narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Dawud ibn Ali, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child of adultery is the worst of the three, if he acts as his parents act."
"10704","10675 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Nattah narrated, Hafs ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir narrated, he said: We entered upon Ishaq ibn Isa ibn Ali in his house, and he narrated to us from his father, from his grandfather, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, had a sitting place with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which he would vacate only for al-Abbas, and that pleased the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One day al-Abbas came, and Abu Bakr moved from his seat for him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What is with you? He said: O Messenger of Allah, your uncle has come. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at him, then turned to Abu Bakr smiling, saying: This is al-Abbas come, wearing white clothes; his children after him shall wear black, and twelve men of them shall rule."
"10705","10676 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, (Ha) and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Hilali narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated, they said: Shayban narrated, from Isa ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blessing of horses is in their sorrel color."
"10706","10677 - Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Dallal al-Kufi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Walid al-Bajali narrated, Faraj ibn Yahya narrated, from Isa ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blessing of horses is in their sorrel color, and most blessed of them in forelock is what is blaze-faced, white-footed, with the right foreleg unmarked."
"10707","10678 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Mazini narrated, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated, my father Sulayman ibn Ali narrated to me, from his father Ali, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever holds his Muslim brother's stirrup, neither hoping from him nor fearing him, shall be forgiven."
"10708","10679 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Shu'ayth ibn Muhriz narrated, Uwayn ibn Amr al-Qaysi narrated, from Ja'far ibn Sulayman ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O Allah, bless my ummah in its early rising on its Thursday."
"10709","10680 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Mazini narrated, Hajjaj ibn Harb al-Shaqari narrated, Sulayman ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Buy slaves and share with them in their provisions - meaning their earnings - and beware of Zanj, for their lives are short and their provisions little."
"10710","10681 - Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-Attar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated, Dawud ibn Ata narrated, Zayd ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting all of Rajab."
"10711","10682 - Abu Amir Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Nahwi al-Suri and Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Bajali narrated, Sulayman ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The people of Paradise are a hundred and twenty rows, eighty of them my ummah."
"10712","10683 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban al-Hashimi narrated, Zaynab bint Sulayman ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated to us, she said: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When I was taken by night, I ended at Sidrat al-Muntaha, and its lote fruits were like large jars."
"10713","10684 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated, al-Mughirah ibn Jamil al-Kindi narrated, Sulayman ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Clientage is neither transferred nor shifted."
"10714","10685 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated, Abdullah ibn al-Simt narrated, Salih ibn Ali al-Hashimi narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: That one of you raise, after a hundred and fifty-four, a puppy, is better for him than raising a child of his loins."
"10715","10686 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, he said: Ibn Abbas would narrate that Allah sent to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) an angel along with the angel Jibril, peace be upon him. The angel said to him: O Muhammad, Allah gives you choice between being a servant-prophet or a king-prophet. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to Jibril as consulting, and he gestured to him to be humble. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather a servant-prophet. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never seen eating reclining till he joined his Lord."
"10716","Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib from Ibn Abbas. 10687 - Al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us, Abu al-Jumahir narrated, Khulayd ibn Da'laj narrated, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever separates from the Muslims a handspan has cast off the bond of Islam from his neck; whoever dies with no imam over him, his death is pre-Islamic; and whoever dies under a blind banner for a faction, or supporting a faction, his killing is pre-Islamic."
"10717","10688 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Aban ibn Yazid narrated, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Messenger of Allah, we are a clan of Rabi'ah, and between us and you are the disbelievers of Mudar; we reach you only in a sacred month. Command us with a matter that if we act upon it we enter Paradise, and we call to it those behind us. He commanded them with four and forbade them four: he commanded them to worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, establish prayer, give zakah, perform hajj of the House, and give the fifth of spoils; and forbade them four: drinking in hantam vessels, dubba, naqir and muzaffat. They said: O Messenger of Allah, from what shall we drink? He said: Upon you are these skins whose mouths are tied."
"10718","10689 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Bakkar al-Dabbi narrated, Abu Hilal narrated, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give glad tidings to those who walk to mosques in darkness of complete light on Resurrection Day."
"10719","10690 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Bakkar narrated, Abu Hilal narrated, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Those who love one another are in Allah's shade."
"10720","10691 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, al-Abbas narrated, Abu Hilal narrated, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah before all things, and There is no god but Allah after all things, shall be protected from worry and sorrow."
"10721","10692 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Shu'bah, Hisham, Aban and Hammam narrated, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas; Hisham stopped it, and the rest raised it, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: One who takes back his gift is like one who returns to his vomit. Hammam added: Qatadah said: We know vomit only as unlawful."
"10722","10693 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Abbas al-Narsi narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated, Sa'id narrated, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who takes back his gift is like one who returns to his vomit."
"10723","10694 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, (Ha) and Abu Shu'ayb Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Bablutti narrated, they said: al-Awza'i narrated, Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to me, Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of one who returns in his charity is as a dog that vomits, then returns to its vomit and eats it."
"10724","10695 - Ibrahim ibn Irq narrated to us, Ibn Musaffa narrated, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There shall not be for us the evil likeness; the likeness of one who returns in his gift is as a dog that returns to its vomit and eats it."
"10725","10696 - Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: One who returns in his gift is as a dog that returns to its vomit."
"10726","10697 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas, that Allah's Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was mentioned Hamzah's daughter, and her beauty mentioned. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you not know she is my brother's daughter through suckling? Do you not know Allah forbade through suckling as He forbade through lineage?"
"10727","10698 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ka'b narrated, Musa ibn Umayr narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's uncle is the twin of his father."
"10728","10699 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Shihab, from Ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed for fingers ten each, and for the hand fifty as obligation."
"10729","10700 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated, from al-Qasim ibn Fayyad, from Khallad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that he heard Ibn Abbas narrate, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was come to by a man seeking fatwa, who had imposed upon himself a badanah in an oath he swore; he gave him fatwa of a badanah of camels, and rebuked the man from returning."
"10730","10701 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, they said: Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated, al-Qasim ibn Fayyad narrated, from Khallad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed people on Friday, a man came to him, stepping over people till he neared him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, establish the hadd upon me. He said: Sit. He sat. Then he stood a second time saying: O Messenger of Allah, establish the hadd upon me. He said: Sit. He sat. Then he stood a third time saying: O Messenger of Allah, establish the hadd upon me. He said: And what is your hadd? He said: I came to a woman unlawfully. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to men of his Companions, among them Ali, Ibn Abbas, Zayd ibn Harithah and Uthman ibn Affan: Go and flog him a hundred - and he had not married. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not flog the one with whom he sinned? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring him to me. When he was brought, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Who is your companion? He said: So-and-so. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to her and called her, asking her about that. She said: He lied; by Allah I do not know him, and I am innocent of what he said; Allah is of the witnesses over what I say. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is your witness that you sinned with her, for she denies you sinned with her; if you have a witness I shall flog her, else I shall flog you the hadd of slander. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have no witness. He ordered concerning him, and he was flogged the hadd of slander, eighty."
"10731","10702 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated, from al-Qasim ibn Fayyad, from Khallad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Jundah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, who heard Ibn Abbas say: A woman said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the reward of a woman's fighting in battle? He said: Obedience to the husband, and acknowledgement of his right."
"10732","10703 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that Umar ibn Abd Allah ibn Jarhad al-Aslami informed him, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The example of one who takes back his gift is like the example of a dog that vomits then returns to its vomit."
"10733","10704 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Bakr ibn Mudar narrated, my father narrated, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The example of one who gives charity then takes it back is like one who vomits then eats from it."
"10734","10705 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Bukayr narrated to him, that he heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The example of one who gives charity then takes back his charity is only like the example of a dog that vomits, then eats its vomit."
"10735","10706 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Abu Hubayrah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept while prostrating until he snored, then he stood and prayed without performing ablution."
"10736","10707 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, they said: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated, my father narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from al-Agharr ibn al-Sabbah, from Khalifah ibn Husayn, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away when he was sixty-three years old."
"10737","10708 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Qirmiti narrated to us, my uncle Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Adawi narrated, Umar ibn Humayd al-Dinawari narrated, Sulayman ibn Arqam narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say the takbir twelve times in the two Eids, seven in the first rak'ah and five in the second, and he used to go by one road and return by another."
"10738","10709 - Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ali ibn Nasr al-Jahdami narrated, Habban ibn Hilal narrated, Sufyan ibn Habib narrated, Ibn Jurayj narrated, from Sa'id ibn Mina, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not drink nabidh older than three days."
"10739","10710 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiy narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated, my father narrated to me, that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to him, from Abd Allah ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried out li'an between al-Ajlani and his wife, and she was pregnant. Her husband said: By Allah, I have not touched her since we stopped watering the date-palms - and al-'afr is watering the date-palms after they are left without watering from the wells for two months - so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make the truth clear. And they claimed that the woman's husband had thin forearms and shanks and reddish hair, and that the one she was accused with was Ibn al-Sahma'. She then gave birth to a black boy with a receding hairline, curly tight hair, thick forearms and stout shanks."
"10740","10711 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zinad informed me, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, the like of this hadith, and he added: Ibn Shaddad said to Ibn Abbas: Is she the woman about whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I stoned anyone without proof I would have stoned her? Ibn Abbas said: No, but that was a woman who had openly committed immorality in Islam."
"10741","10712 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, that Abd Allah ibn Shaddad said to Ibn Abbas, mentioning the two who invoked li'an: Is she the woman about whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I stoned anyone without proof I would have stoned her? Ibn Abbas said: No, that was a woman who committed openly."
"10742","10713 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Umar ibn Ali narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Uqbah, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried out li'an between a man and his wife."
"10743","10714 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Abbas, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have had no contact with my wife since the 'afar of the date-palms - and their 'afar is that they are pollinated then left forty days without watering after pollination - and I found a man with my wife. The husband was yellowish, thin-limbed, with straight hair, while the one she was accused with was darkish, curly-haired and stout. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make clear, O Allah, make clear, then he carried out li'an between them, and she gave birth to a child resembling the one she was accused with."
"10744","10715 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiy narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Abbas, that he mentioned the two who invoked li'an in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Asim said something about it then left, then a man of his people came to him and mentioned that he had found a man with his wife. Asim said: I have only been afflicted with this because of what I said. He took him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of what he had found his wife in. That man was yellowish, thin-fleshed, with straight hair, while the one he claimed to have found with his wife was reddish and fleshy. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make clear. She gave birth to one resembling the one her husband mentioned he had found with her, so the Messenger of Allah carried out li'an between them. A man in the gathering said to Ibn Abbas: Is she the one about whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I stoned a woman without proof I would have stoned this one? Ibn Abbas said: No, that was a woman who used to display immorality in Islam."
"10745","10716 - Tahir ibn Isa ibn Qayras al-Misri narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah informed me, and Abu al-Jarud Mas'ud ibn Muhammad al-Ramli narrated to us, Imran ibn Harun al-Sufi narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I stoned anyone without proof I would have stoned so-and-so woman; suspicion has become apparent in her appearance, her speech, and those who visit her."
"10746","10717 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ufayr narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forgot the Zuhr and Asr prayers on the day of al-Ahzab, and remembered after Maghrib. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They kept us from prayer until the day was gone; may Allah fill their graves with fire. Then he prayed them after Maghrib."
"10747","10718 - Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ufayr narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out with a lock of false hair and said: The women of the Children of Israel used to put this in their hair, so they were cursed and mosques were made forbidden to them."
"10748","10719 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, and Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Waki' narrated, both from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: I wish people would reduce from a third to a fourth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A third, and a third is much - or large."
"10749","10720 - Ahmad ibn Mutayr narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus al-Fakhuri narrated, Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated, Yunus narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: Mut'ah was indeed practiced in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10750","10721 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Sa'id ibn Kathir ibn Dinar al-Himsi narrated, my father narrated, Shu'ayb ibn Zurayq narrated, from Ata al-Khurasani who said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr said: Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr was in the ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah while Ibn Abbas was sitting forbidding mut'ah in Hajj. Ibn Abbas called out to him: We know better about that; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did that, and men dissolved ihram and enjoyed Umrah, having no sacrificial animals with them, and they circumambulated the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and approached women. Then Ibn Abbas said: Yes, I give fatwa to that effect, on account of what was done in the time of the Imam of the God-fearing. Ibn al-Zubayr said: Expose yourself to it, for by Allah, if you do it I will surely stone you with your own stones. Then their exchange ended."
"10751","10722 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abd Allah who said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah bint al-Harith while he was in ihram."
"10752","10723 - Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah who said: Ibn Abbas used to narrate that Abu Bakr uncovered the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while it was covered with a cloth, looked at the face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then bent over him and kissed him."
"10753","10724 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated, Yazid ibn Iyad narrated, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi narrated, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Ibn Abbas who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat meat from a sheep's shoulder, then pray without performing ablution."
"10754","10725 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Rawh ibn Salah narrated, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abu Salamah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he was asked about drawing lines for divination, and he said: It is a remnant of knowledge."
"10755","10726 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Shayban narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Ibn Abbas and A'ishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in Makkah ten years with the Qur'an descending upon him, and in Madinah ten years with it descending upon him."
"10756","10727 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mawsili narrated, they said: Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Ibn Abbas, regarding: And he certainly saw him in another descent: he said: He saw his Lord, mighty and majestic."
"10757","10728 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated, Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah al-Umawi narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Usayd, from Abu Salamah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Women have no share in the marriage contract itself; Maymunah entrusted her affair to Umm al-Fadl, Umm al-Fadl entrusted it to al-Abbas, and he married her to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10758","10729 - Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, from his father, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Zakat al-Fitr: a sa' of dates, or a sa' of barley, or two mudds of wheat, upon every resident and nomad, young and old, free and slave."
"10759","10730 - Abu Sa'id Ja'far ibn Sunayd ibn Dawud narrated to us, my father narrated, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, Ibn Abi Mulaykah informed me, that Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman informed him, that Marwan said: Go, O Abu Rafi' - to his doorkeeper - to Ibn Abbas. It was said to him: If every one of us who rejoices in what he has been given and loves to be praised for what he does will be punished, we will all be punished. Ibn Abbas said: What have you to do with this? This was only revealed about the People of the Book. Then Ibn Abbas recited: And when Allah took the covenant of those who were given the Book: you shall make it clear to people, up to His saying: Think not that those who rejoice in what they have done and love to be praised for what they did not do. And Ibn Abbas said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked them about something, so they envied him, concealed it and told him other than the truth. They rejoiced and left having shown him that they had told him what he asked them about, sought his praise thereby, and rejoiced in what they had attained of concealing from him what he had asked them."
"10760","10731 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated, from his father, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never aided in any place as he was aided at Uhud. That was objected to, so Ibn Abbas said: Between me and whoever objects is the Book of Allah. Allah says: And Allah certainly fulfilled His promise to you when you were killing them by His permission. Ibn Abbas said: Al-hass means killing. Until when you lost heart, up to His saying: And He has pardoned you, and Allah is full of bounty to the believers. He meant by this the archers. That is because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stationed them at an ambush post then said: Guard our backs; if you see us being killed, do not aid us, and if you see us having taken spoils, do not share with us. When Allah granted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoils and gave him free hand over the camp of the polytheists, all the archers left and entered the camp plundering, while the ranks of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had become interlocked like this - and he interlaced his right and left fingers. When the archers vacated that position they had been in, the cavalry entered from that spot against the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so they struck one another, and many Muslims were killed. From the start of the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions had killed seven or nine of the standard-bearers of the polytheists. The Muslims made a move toward the cavalry but did not reach where people say, the cave; they were only beneath al-Mihras. Satan shouted: Muhammad has been killed, and we did not doubt that it was true. We remained not doubting that he had indeed been killed, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appeared between the two mountain passes, and I recognized him by his leaning gait when he walked. We rejoiced until it was as if what had struck us had not struck us. He climbed toward us saying: Allah's wrath has intensified against people who bloodied the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And at another time he would say: O Allah, they have no right to overcome us so as to reach us. He stayed a while, when Abu Sufyan shouted from the foot of the mountain: Rise high, Hubal - meaning his idol - where is the son of Abu Kabshah, where is the son of Abu Quhafah, where is the son of al-Khattab? Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not answer him? He said: Yes. When he said: Rise high, Hubal, Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Allah is higher and more majestic. Abu Sufyan said: O son of al-Khattab, you have done a favor. He repeated the like of it, saying: Where is the son of Abu Kabshah, where is the son of Abu Quhafah, where is the son of al-Khattab? Umar said: Here is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), here is Abu Bakr, and here am I, Umar. Abu Sufyan said: A day for the day of Badr; days alternate, and war is in turns. Umar said: Not equal; our slain are in Paradise and your slain are in the Fire. He said: You claim that; then we have failed and lost. Then Abu Sufyan said: You will find among your slain mutilation, though that was not by the counsel of our chiefs; then the zeal of Jahiliyyah overtook him and he said: Yet it happened, and we did not dislike it."
"10761","10732 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated, from his father, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed, they are the disbelievers, the wrongdoers, the defiantly disobedient. Ibn Abbas said: He revealed it about two groups of Jews, one of which had dominated the other in the Jahiliyyah until they agreed and settled that for every slain man the mighty group killed of the humble group the blood-money would be fifty wasqs, and for every slain man the humble group killed of the mighty group it would be one hundred wasqs. They remained so until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and both groups submitted to the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), though the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had not yet prevailed over them nor trodden them down; it was a truce. Then the humble group killed a man of the mighty group, so the mighty group sent to the humble group: send us one hundred wasqs. The humble group said: Did this ever happen? Their religion is one and their lineage is one; the blood-money of some being half that of others? We only gave you this as oppression from you against us out of fear of you. Now that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has come, we shall not give you that. War almost erupted between them, then they agreed to make the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judge between them. The mighty group reflected and said: By Allah, Muhammad will not give you from them double what he gives them from you; they spoke truly, they only gave us this out of oppression and domination over them. So send to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) someone to learn his opinion for you; if he gives you what you want, appoint him judge, and if he does not, beware of him and do not appoint him. They sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) some hypocrites to test the opinion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for them. When they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah informed His Messenger of all their affair and what they intended, and Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: O Messenger, let not those grieve you who hasten into disbelief among those who say, up to His saying: And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed, they are the defiantly disobedient. Then he said: By Allah, about them it was revealed, and them Allah meant."
"10762","10733 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Huti narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated, and Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated, they said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated, from his father, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his sword Dhu al-Faqar as an extra spoil on the day of Badr, and it is the one about which he saw the dream on the day of Uhud."
"10763","10734 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father and Ishaq ibn Bakr ibn Mudar narrated, and Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, they said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, from Irak ibn Malik, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The moon split in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10764","10735 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah al-Khallal al-Marwazi narrated, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Yazid ibn Habib, from Irak ibn Malik, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in Makkah in the year of the Conquest fifteen days shortening the prayer."
"10765","10736 - Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Waki'i narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ja'far ibn Awn narrated, from Abu al-Umays, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Jahm, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The last surah revealed of the Qur'an in full was: When comes the help of Allah and the victory."
"10766","10737 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abu Salih and Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, they said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Qasamah existed in the Jahiliyyah as a restraint among people; whoever swore a binding oath in which he sinned was shown a punishment from Allah made an example for daring against sacred things, so they used to avoid binding oaths and fear them. When Allah sent Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he affirmed qasamah, and the Muslims were the most cautious about it because of what Allah had taught them of that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged with qasamah between two clans of the Ansar called Banu Harithah: the Jews had killed Muhayyisah and the Jews denied it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) summoned the Jews for their qasamah, since they were the ones against whom the blood claim was made, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to swear fifty oaths, fifty men, that they were innocent of his killing, but the Jews declined the oaths. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) summoned Banu Harithah and ordered them to swear fifty oaths, fifty men, that the Jews had killed him treacherously and thereby establish the claim against the one they alleged had killed their companion, but Banu Harithah declined the oaths. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, he judged his blood-money against the Jews, since he was found among them and in their dwellings."
"10767","10738 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated, Nuh ibn Darraj narrated, from al-Ajlah ibn Abd Allah, from Zayd ibn Ali, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: When word reached the companions of Ali, as they marched to Basrah, that the people of Basrah had gathered behind Talhah and al-Zubayr, it distressed them and weighed on their hearts. Ali said: By Him besides whom there is no god, he shall surely prevail over the people of Basrah, Talhah and al-Zubayr shall surely be killed, and there shall surely come out to you from Kufah six thousand five hundred and fifty men - or five thousand five hundred and fifty men, al-Ajlah doubted. Ibn Abbas said: That weighed on my mind, so when the people of Kufah came I went out and said: I shall see; if it is as he says, then it is a matter he heard, otherwise it is a trick of war. I met a man of the army and asked him, and by Allah he had barely finished before he said what Ali had said. Ibn Abbas said: And it is of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to inform him of."
"10768","10739 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated, from Sufyan, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that Mu'awiyah came disputing about the mut'ah of Hajj, and Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did it."
"10769","10740 - Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Junday Saburi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated, he said: I heard my father, Abu Hamzah narrated, from Jabir, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept until his snoring was heard, then he stood and prayed without purification."
"10770","10741 - al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Massisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated, Hushaym narrated, Jabir al-Ju'fi informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ali Abu Ja'far, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out intending prayer, passed by a cooking pot, took a bone from it and ate it, then went on to prayer without performing ablution."
"10771","10742 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated, my father narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Ibn Abbas, that a questioner asked him: O Abu al-Abbas, is there repentance for a killer? Ibn Abbas said as if astonished at his affair: What are you saying? He repeated the question to him, and he said to him: What are you saying? Two or three times. Then Ibn Abbas said: How can he have repentance? I heard your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The slain man shall come holding his head in one of his hands, seizing his killer with his other hand, his jugular veins gushing blood, until he brings him to the Throne. The slain man shall say to Allah: Lord, this one killed me. Allah, mighty and majestic, shall say to the killer: May you perish, and he shall be taken to the Fire."
"10772","10743 - Ali ibn Abd Allah and Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, they said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Malik ibn Anas, from Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The previously married woman has more right to herself than her guardian, and the virgin's consent is her silence."
"10773","10744 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated, from Malik ibn Anas, from Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"10774","10745 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated, and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar narrated, they said: Sufyan narrated, Ziyad ibn Sa'd and Malik ibn Anas narrated, from Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The previously married woman has more right to herself than her guardian, and the virgin's father shall seek her permission; her silence is her consent."
"10775","10746 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated, from Yazid ibn Iyad and Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The previously married woman has more authority over herself, and the virgin shall be asked permission regarding herself, and her permission is her silence."
"10776","10747 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Isa ibn Yunus narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawhab narrated, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The previously married woman has more right to herself than her guardian, and the virgin shall be consulted, and her silence is her consent."
"10777","10748 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Makki narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Hakim ibn Hakim, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a woman of Khath'am came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is a very old man who has become senile, and Allah's obligation of Hajj has reached him while he cannot perform it; will it suffice for him if I perform it on his behalf? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes."
"10778","10749 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Huti narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated, Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most hateful of people to Allah is one who seeks in Islam a practice of the Jahiliyyah, and one who seeks the blood of a man without right in order to shed his blood."
"10779","10750 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated, Shu'ayb narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: Musaylimah the Liar came in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: If Muhammad assigns the rule after him to me, I shall follow him; and he had come to it with many people of his folk. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him, accompanied by Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, with a piece of palm stalk in the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He stood over Musaylimah among his companions and said: Had you asked me for this piece I would not have given it to you; you shall not exceed Allah's decree concerning you. If you turn away, Allah shall destroy you. I indeed see you as the one I saw in my vision, and this Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas shall answer you on my behalf. And he turned away."
"10780","10751 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated, Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah informed us, from Ibn Abi Husayn, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, said: The son of Adam denied Me, though he had no right to deny Me, and he insulted Me, though he had no right to do so. As for his denial of Me, it is his claim that I cannot restore him as he was; as for his insult of Me, it is his saying that I have a son. Glory be to Me above taking a wife or a son."
"10781","10752 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Sufyan narrated, and Ali ibn Jabalah al-Asbahani narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Hafs narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah, from Hakim ibn Hakim ibn Abbad ibn Hunayf, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, led me in prayer at the House twice. He led me in Zuhr when the sun declined, when a shadow was the measure of a sandal strap; then he led me in Asr when the shadow of everything was equal to it; then he led me in Maghrib when the fasting person breaks fast; then he led me in Isha when the twilight disappeared; then he led me in Fajr when food and drink become forbidden to the fasting person. Then he led me in Zuhr the next day when everything was equal to its shadow; then he led me in Asr when everything was twice its shadow; then he led me in Maghrib at the same time when the fasting person breaks fast; then he led me in Isha when the first third of the night had gone; then he led me in Fajr - Abu Nu'aym said: I do not know what he said about Fajr - then he turned to me and said: O Muhammad, this is the time of the prophets before you; the time is between these two times."
"10782","10753 - Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri and Ibn Abi Sabrah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah, Hakim ibn Hakim narrated to me, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril led me in prayer at the House and led me in Zuhr. Then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Abu Nu'aym, and said at the end of the hadith: Then he led me in Fajr at daybreak."
"10783","10754 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiy narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Hakim ibn Hakim, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"10784","10755 - Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Umar ibn Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, from Ibn Abbas: Jibril came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned the like of the hadith of al-Thawri. Abu al-Qasim said: Ibn Uqdah and al-Walid ibn Aban wrote this hadith down from me; al-Dabari is alone in transmitting it - meaning the hadith of Abd Allah ibn Umar."
"10785","10756 - Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrate, from his maternal uncle, who said: Ibn Abbas, on Friday, would have a place spread for him in the house of Maymunah where he would converse. A man said to him: Tell me about what fire has touched. Ibn Abbas said: I shall only tell you what I saw of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He and his companions were in his house when the caller to prayer came, so he stood for prayer; when he reached the door, a tray with bread and meat was brought, so he returned with his companions and ate, and they ate, then he returned to prayer without performing ablution. The maternal uncle of Ibn Ishaq is Musa ibn Yasar."
"10786","10757 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed me, that Sulayman ibn Yasar informed him, that he heard Ibn Abbas, and he saw Abu Hurayrah performing ablution and said: Do you know, my young Ibn Abbas, what I am performing ablution for? He said: I performed ablution for some dried yoghurt crumbs I ate. Ibn Abbas said: I do not care what you perform ablution for; I bear witness that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat a shoulder of meat, then stand for prayer without performing ablution. He said: Sulayman was present at that exchange between them."
"10787","10758 - Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated, from Malik ibn Anas, and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir narrated, and Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun, and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated, all of them from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to prayer and was brought a shoulder of meat, which he bit into, then went on to prayer without rinsing his mouth or purifying himself; the wording is that of the hadith of Rawh ibn al-Qasim."
"10788","10759 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khallad ibn Yahya narrated, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar who said: Ibn Abbas said: Shall I not show you how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution? He called for a vessel with water, scooped a handful and rinsed his mouth and sniffed water, then took another and joined his hands with it and washed his face, then took another and washed his right hand, then scooped another handful and washed his left hand, then took a grasp of water, lowered his hand and wiped his head and ears with it, then scooped another handful and sprinkled it over his feet with sandals on them, and the left likewise, and wiped the undersides of the sandals, then said: Like this."
"10789","10760 - Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-Attar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman and Abd Allah, the two sons of Zayd ibn Aslam, narrated to me, from their father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that Arbad ibn Qays ibn Juzayy ibn Khalid ibn Ja'far ibn Kilab and Amir ibn al-Tufayl ibn Malik came to Madinah to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was sitting and sat before him. Amir ibn al-Tufayl said: O Muhammad, what will you grant me if I accept Islam? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For you is what is for the Muslims, and upon you is what is upon them. Amir ibn al-Tufayl said: Will you grant me the rule after you if I accept Islam? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is not for you nor for your people, but for you is the command of the cavalry. He said: I am now in command of the cavalry of Najd; grant me the desert and yours the towns. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No. When he turned away from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Amir said: By Allah, I shall surely fill it against you with horses and men. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah shall restrain you. When Arbad and Amir left, Amir said: O Arbad, I shall distract Muhammad from you with talk, so strike him with the sword; if you kill Muhammad, the people will do no more than accept blood-money and dislike war, so we shall pay them the blood-money. Arbad said: I shall do it. They returned to him, and Amir said: O Muhammad, stand with me so I may speak to you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood with him, and they withdrew to the wall, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing with him speaking to him, while Arbad drew his sword; when he put his hand on the hilt, his hand stiffened upon it and he could not draw the sword. Arbad was slow in striking Amir's blow, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned, saw Arbad and what he was doing, and left them. When Amir and Arbad left the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until they were at al-Harrah, the Harrah of Waqim, they alighted, and Sa'd ibn Mu'adh and Usayd ibn Hudayr came out to them and said: Be gone, O enemies of Allah, may Allah curse you. Amir said: Who is this, O Sa'd? He said: This is Usayd ibn Hudayr the scribe. They went on until they were at al-Raqm, when Allah, mighty and majestic, sent a thunderbolt upon Arbad and killed him. Amir went on until he was at al-Harr, then Allah sent a swelling upon him which seized him, and night overtook him in the house of a woman of Banu Salul. He kept touching the swelling in his throat, saying: A gland like a camel's gland, in the house of a Saluliyyah woman, begrudging that he should die in her house. Then he mounted his horse and rode it hard until he died upon it on his way back. Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed about them: Allah knows what every female bears and what the wombs diminish, up to His saying: And they have no protector besides Him. He said: Successive angels by Allah's command guarding Muhammad. Then he mentioned Arbad and what befell him, saying: It is He who shows you lightning in fear and hope, up to His saying: And He is severe in assault."
"10790","10761 - Muhammad ibn Ya'qub ibn Surah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when brought fruit, would give it to the youngest of the children present."
"10791","10762 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated to us, my father narrated, and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated, they said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate from a sheep's shoulder, then prayed without performing ablution."
"10792","10763 - Zakariyya al-Saji narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Harun Abu Alqamah al-Farwi narrated, Qudamah ibn Muhammad al-Ashja'i narrated, from Makhramah ibn Bukayr, from his father, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mark between us and the hypocrites is that they do not drink Zamzam to fullness."
"10793","10764 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Harun al-Farwi narrated, Qudamah narrated, from Makhramah ibn Bukayr, from his father, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contest except in a camel's foot, a hoof, or an arrowhead."
"10794","10765 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym Dirar ibn Surad narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Safwan ibn Sulaym and Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, what is allowed me of my wife while she is menstruating? He said: She ties her waist-wrapper, then do with her as you wish."
"10795","10766 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq and Hajjaj ibn Imran narrated to us, they said: Amr ibn al-Husayn al-Uqayli narrated, Yahya ibn al-Ala narrated, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked in the mirror he would say: Praise be to Allah who made my form good and adorned in me what He disfigured in others. When he applied kohl he would put two in each eye and one between them. When he dressed he would begin with the right, and when he undressed he would take off the left. When he entered the mosque he would enter his right foot, and he loved beginning with the right in everything, when taking and when giving."
"10796","10767 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated, from Sa'id ibn Khalid, from Isma'il ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out while they were sitting and said: Shall I not tell you of the best of people in rank? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A man holding the head of his horse - or he said: a horse - in the path of Allah, or he is killed. He said: Shall I tell you of the one next to him? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A man withdrawn in a mountain ravine, establishing prayer, giving zakat, and keeping away from people's evils. Shall I tell you of the worst of people? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: One who is asked by Allah and does not give for His sake."
"10797","10768 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Bukayr narrated to him, from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Shall I not tell you of the best of people? Among the best of people is a man holding his horse's reins in the path of Allah. Shall I tell you of the one after him? One withdrawn among his sheep, discharging Allah's due regarding them. And shall I tell you of the worst of people? A man asked by Allah who does not give for His sake."
"10798","10769 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn Marjanah, who informed him, that Abd Allah ibn Umar recited this verse: And whether you disclose what is in yourselves or hide it, Allah shall call you to account for it; He forgives whom He wills and punishes whom He wills. His eyes shed tears, and that reached Ibn Abbas, who said: May Allah forgive Abu Abd al-Rahman; by my life, this verse concerned the Muslims before him, until Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: Allah does not burden a soul beyond its capacity; it has what it earned and against it what it acquired. He said: Whisperings are what people cannot control, and Allah decreed for every soul recompense according to what it earned."
"10799","10770 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, and Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Attar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated, they said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, from al-Qasim ibn Harran al-Khawlani, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn Marjanah who said: I was with Ibn Umar when he read: To Allah belongs what is in the heavens and what is on earth; and whether you disclose what is in yourselves or hide it, Allah shall call you to account for it. Ibn Umar sobbed until Ibn Abbas heard his sobbing at the back of the mosque. Ibn Umar said: We shall be taken to task for what our souls whisper. Sa'id ibn Marjanah said: I asked Ibn Abbas about what I had witnessed and told him, and he said: May Allah forgive Abu Abd al-Rahman; the Muslims found in this verse the like of what he found, and complained of it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Thus said your Lord, so say: We believe in what was sent down, we heard and obeyed; Your forgiveness, our Lord, and to You is the return. They said it as long as Allah willed them to say it, until Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: The Messenger believes in what was sent down to him from his Lord, up to His saying: Allah does not burden a soul beyond its capacity."
"10800","10771 - Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Ayyub al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Wasil Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated, Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Bunani narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pulpits of gold shall be set for the prophets and they shall sit upon them, while my pulpit remains and I do not sit upon it - or he said: I do not sit down upon it - standing before my Lord occupied with my community, fearing lest I be sent to Paradise while my community remains after me. I shall say: Lord, my community, my community. Allah the Exalted shall say: O Muhammad, what do you want Me to do with your community? I shall say: Lord, settle their reckoning quickly. They shall be summoned and reckoned; among them is one who enters Paradise by Allah's mercy, and among them is one who enters Paradise by my intercession. I shall continue to intercede until I am given documents of men already sent to the Fire, until Malik, keeper of the Fire, says: O Muhammad, you have left nothing of your Lord's wrath against your community to be avenged."
